{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe","id":299851,"title":"Red Talons, the throw-away tribe?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-02T01:41:27-08:00","id":299851,"title":"Red Talons, the throw-away tribe?","content":"(Note, in this, I'm discussing the general things I've seen in online forum gaming and here. I know a lot of the veterans here DO use Talons well, so this is mostly speaking in general)<br /> <br /> One thing I've noticed a lot in online games and discussions, is that as far as Red Talons are considered, they tend to be strawmen(wolves?), fallen tribe for sure or non-existant entirely. Now, I understand in part this, lupus are hard to play, lupus who don't even want to understand humanity are harder.<br /> <br /> Yet, I feel they should be present and their opinions heard more in games. Because Glass Walkers, their opposite is very popular indeed. And I think that skews the games massively as most games are set in cities and often Talons are banned. While this is true in canon, it game terms it also makes them look stupid. And if a well played Talon comes in-game, its often seen as backwards or stupid.<br /> <br /> And I think that takes away what makes the Walker vs Talon conflict so interesting, the fact that -both- are extremes on the Garou. By having no Talons or strawman ones, their side is not heard. And I think it should, because Talons are a reminder of the wild in garou, untouched by human culture. They have a great tribebook about how they deal with the wilds and spirits and handle the changing world. Not well, but they are far from ignorant or stupid. And without that voice, only the Glass Walker one is heard and so their extremity to human side is harder to see.<br /> <br /> So, I ask those who rarely use the Red Talons, what would make them more playable or something to be used more?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:33:15-08:00","id":299872,"title":"","content":"I think the biggest problem with the Red Talons is that while they are the Glasswalker's opposites in themes, lots of Tribes can fit the role they play without being inherently burdened by the whole anti-homid deal. A Wendigo or Get lupus can just as easily be the big bad wolf that has disdain for humanity. Pretty much any tribe besides the Glasswalkers can have a lupus that plays the &quot;more in touch with nature&quot; side of the argument.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with the Talons. They're extremists for a side that is exceedingly well represented in the Garou Nation as a whole. The Glasswalkers are extremists for the side that is under represented amongst the other Tribes. A good example would be that nobody gets a Renown knock for being more wolfish, but everyone except the Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers get a renown hit for being to Weaverish.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons need something more than being not Homid and pro-nature that isn't, &quot;we're more angry about it and more readily violent about it than anyone else.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:38:03-08:00","id":299877,"title":"","content":"I've started this thought experiment. I can't stand the Talons. I don't think I would ever play one unless the ST asked me to because s/he needed said role to be filled. With that said, how could they fit in? Are you looking for character concepts? Are you intending to run/play in city campaigns?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:44:24-08:00","id":299881,"title":"","content":"Playing unorthodox Red Talon would be more interested, but canonically you should be treated like a near Ronin or defector for expressing opinion that humans have SOME merit. Someone treated like that would probably sooner indeed defect to a tribe to which said Garou is closer ideologically than suffer ostracism from peers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:46:10-08:00","id":299882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299872#post299872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the biggest problem with the Red Talons is that while they are the Glasswalker's opposites in themes, lots of Tribes can fit the role they play without being inherently burdened by the whole anti-homid deal. A Wendigo or Get lupus can just as easily be the big bad wolf that has disdain for humanity. Pretty much any tribe besides the Glasswalkers can have a lupus that plays the &quot;more in touch with nature&quot; side of the argument.<br /> <br /> That's the problem with the Talons. They're extremists for a side that is exceedingly well represented in the Garou Nation as a whole. The Glasswalkers are extremists for the side that is under represented amongst the other Tribes. A good example would be that nobody gets a Renown knock for being more wolfish, but everyone except the Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers get a renown hit for being to Weaverish.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, from what I've seen, the opposite is true. Most PCs even from non-urrah tribes have much more common with the Walkers than Talons. The Anti-human lupus are almost unheard of, if there even ARE any lupus. By play, the Glass Walker side is much more popular and represented, while the Talon side is barely there if at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299877#post299877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've started this thought experiment. I can't stand the Talons. I don't think I would ever play one unless the ST asked me to because s/he needed said role to be filled. With that said, how could they fit in? Are you looking for character concepts? Are you intending to run/play in city campaigns?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just asking in general why they tend to be ignored so much and what could be done to fix the situation for them. Just a curiosity and a thought experiment. And also to consider if I ever put up a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T04:43:43-08:00","id":299915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299872#post299872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's the problem with the Talons. They're extremists for a side that is exceedingly well represented in the Garou Nation as a whole. The Glasswalkers are extremists for the side that is under represented amongst the other Tribes. A good example would be that nobody gets a Renown knock for being more wolfish, but everyone except the Glasswalkers and Bone Gnawers get a renown hit for being to Weaverish.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons need something more than being not Homid and pro-nature that isn't, &quot;we're more angry about it and more readily violent about it than anyone else.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That is....not my experience, to put it mildly. And I've played a few Talons, also used them as NPCs a lot.<br /> <br /> The notion that humans are wyrm tainted and should either be exterminated or at best brought back to &quot;controllable&quot; population levels is NOT something that is &quot;exceedingly well represented in the Garou Nation as a whole&quot;. For starters, all the other Tribes have homid Kinfolk (usually more than lupus). This means a Get lupus CANNOT hold this position at all, since it basically means he wants to kill over half of his own Kinfolk, which would be.....odd at best.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing unorthodox Red Talon would be more interested, but canonically you should be treated like a near Ronin or defector for expressing opinion that humans have SOME merit. Someone treated like that would probably sooner indeed defect to a tribe to which said Garou is closer ideologically than suffer ostracism from peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they wouldn't be treated as near-Ronin. They'd be treated the way the Whelp's compromise is (since that's what they would be), which is exactly like any other camp within the other tribes. Griffin himself clearly accepts these Garou as Red Talons, or they would simply not be, so they are nowhere near Ronin.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T05:30:52-08:00","id":299924,"title":"","content":"Still treated with disdain by more radical tribeswolves most likely even if their tribe totem clearly is more reasonable than some of Red Talons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:08:39-08:00","id":299935,"title":"","content":"Where's the line before Griffin goes &quot;GTFO!&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:23:44-08:00","id":299946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Where's the line before Griffin goes &quot;GTFO!&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I think it's going full &quot;reverse furry&quot; and going all homid wannabee like otaku pretending they are Japanese. Certainly that would be crossing a line.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:37:09-08:00","id":299950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299946#post299946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's going full &quot;reverse furry&quot; and going all homid wannabee like otaku pretending they are Japanese. Certainly that would be crossing a line.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it would take a semi-special snowflake to be one in a city campaign? If said Talon was running around with a city pack and not fulfilling Griffin's obligations, would that Talon still be part of his tribe?<br /> <br /> I find the Talons unusually boring. It's my opinion. However, if asked, or perhaps it may fit, I might play one. Perhaps some kind of cowed cub who, with Shadow Lord-like fervor, would be waiting and planning to overturn the pack's hierarchy. Hopefully such concept wouldn't be disruptive. Maybe a Talon Ragabash that does a lot of indecent, shocking things in homid form, such as flashing women in the park, scratch cars, set fire to... whatever. Just doing the thought experiment, here.<br /> <br /> Edited to add: I'm sure someone out there has thought of a camp for Glass Walkers that mocks the Talons that has the totem of &quot;Peter Griffin&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4123,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","user":"Rall Bashir","date":". 11-02-2014, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:41:13-08:00","id":299951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe a Talon Ragabash that does a lot of indecent, shocking things in homid form, such as flashing women in the park, scratch cars, set fire to... whatever. Just doing the thought experiment, here. </div> </div> </div>Please let us not verge into fishmalk territory. My perspective on Ragabash is that they contest traditions in actually meaningful way, in my opinion. I could imagine a Talon Ragabash who is still pretty distrustful of humans but maybe he sees some merit in humans or perceives that they can improve without excessive violence on part of Talons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:55:54-08:00","id":299953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299935#post299935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where's the line before Griffin goes &quot;GTFO!&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Be homid. That's the <i>sole</i> criterion. Be homid.<br /> <br /> As noted, philosophically, Griffin doesn't appear to care what a Talon thinks, he only cares what breed a Talon was born. Metis are rarely, and grudgingly, accepted. A Talon with some homid ancestry may not be liked by other Talons, depending on the sept, but they're still part of the tribe (it's a Merit in the Revised Tribebook). Actually being homid, however, is a no-go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T06:56:00-08:00","id":299954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299946#post299946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's going full &quot;reverse furry&quot; and going all homid wannabee like otaku pretending they are Japanese. Certainly that would be crossing a line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299950#post299950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, it would take a semi-special snowflake to be one in a city campaign? If said Talon was running around with a city pack and not fulfilling Griffin's obligations, would that Talon still be part of his tribe?<br /> <br /> I find the Talons unusually boring. It's my opinion. However, if asked, or perhaps it may fit, I might play one. Perhaps some kind of cowed cub who, with Shadow Lord-like fervor, would be waiting and planning to overturn the pack's hierarchy. Hopefully such concept wouldn't be disruptive. Maybe a Talon Ragabash that does a lot of indecent, shocking things in homid form, such as flashing women in the park, scratch cars, set fire to... whatever. Just doing the thought experiment, here.<br /> <br /> Edited to add: I'm sure someone out there has thought of a camp for Glass Walkers that mocks the Talons that has the totem of &quot;Peter Griffin&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you both are thinking of the situation a bit too human based. The absence of humanity is not absence of morality, so to speak.<br /> <br /> A Red Talon that doesn't see all humans as wyrm tainted and to be slaughtered would still possibly try to direct humanity towards mora natural way of life. That is, fear the wilds and try to live more in harmony with nature, even if that includes being killed by it.<br /> <br /> They would also not try to overturn hieracy of the pack just because they disagree with the leader, a pack has to function well together and a Talon is far more likely to follow orders from the leader than many homid or metis just because the leader ordered. If they feel the leaders actions are damaging to the pack or Gaia, they would challenge the leader. Whether on the mound or simply in a combat, to see who is stronger and better.<br /> <br /> As for the shock tactics, why would a lupus care for it? Why bother shocking the apes that can't even hear Gaia's voice, when a better way would be to show them their place as prey? Chasing the human around the city, leaving calling cards in their apartment and killing their pets is much stronger. It tells the human it is never safe and if the Talon chooses, prey. Even if the Talon never chooses to do anything, it is still a powerful message.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Though, back to the main question of the thread; Why are the Talons boring, why are the wilds they live in boring? That in itself is part of WtA's world, yet it so easily gets pushed aside in favour of the cities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 11-02-2014, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T07:04:18-08:00","id":299958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299954#post299954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the shock tactics, why would a lupus care for it? Why bother shocking the apes that can't even hear Gaia's voice, when a better way would be to show them their place as prey? Chasing the human around the city, leaving calling cards in their apartment and killing their pets is much stronger. It tells the human it is never safe and if the Talon chooses, prey. Even if the Talon never chooses to do anything, it is still a powerful message.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually awesome, and should I ever play a Talon, I'll steal that idea. I don't deny my ignorance of this game.<br /> <br /> Also &quot;fishmalk&quot;? Is that what we used to call &quot;Teddybears&quot;, on account of whenever they came to play, they'd have a teddybear and go &quot;Look at me, I'm a Malkavian! See? I have toys!&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T07:22:28-08:00","id":299965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think you both are thinking of the situation a bit too human based. The absence of humanity is not absence of morality, so to speak. </div> </div> </div>Basically my post was somewhat ironical rather than full on serious.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The absence of humanity is not absence of morality, so to speak. </div> </div> </div>Morality is subjective in the sense that what is moral to another may not be moral to other being.<br /> <br /> Of course, if morality of somebody involves me getting slaughtered potentially, I will contest that and likely not feel bad about killing in self-defense while I won't decree my or anyone's morality as objective.<br /> <br /> But if some of them were willing, you know, to sit down and have a talk between two different species without it ending in automatic bloodshed, I would be also more than willing to sit down too, listen to their warnings of supernatural evil being a threat to both species, and who knows, maybe I would even invite them to a homemade dinner that is ecologically friendly even according to strictest standards because my rabbits have plenty free space to go around and they eat only natural food. Just let's be good neighbors, though please don't kill those local members of hunter club because I prefer political means of cracking down on them. Probably any reasonable Garou PC would not get an Ally dot because of befriending me, because let's face, I have no political power, but sure, I can donate money to ecological organisation that is front for Garou or sign an initiative.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should probably make a thread what fun things you would with your Garou friends in spare time that would not be culturally insensitive.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-02-2014, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T08:12:34-08:00","id":300008,"title":"","content":"The Revised Red Talons Tribebook noted that there are actually an awful lot of places in the wilderness that aren't so pure even though no human ever came to them. And the Red Talons are the only ones that live deep enough in said wilderness to bump into them and who have to deal with them. After all, it's not as if there was industrialization to spawn monsters back in the days where they came out of caves. Because they're being driven into dangerous and marginal habitats, they're going to be a bit resentful at the very least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299965#post299965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically my post was somewhat ironical rather than full on serious.</div> </div> </div> </div>One day, you may find that the mask doesn't come off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Morality is subjective in the sense that what is moral to another may not be moral to other being.<br /> <br /> Of course, if morality of somebody involves me getting slaughtered potentially, I will contest that and likely not feel bad about killing in self-defense while I won't decree my or anyone's morality as objective. </div> </div> </div>Flipside - wolves, the only Kin to the Talons, are hemmed in and in far greater danger of dying out completely. For the Red Talons, human extirpation is the logical end conclusion of a need for aggressive self-defense. Humans, to the experience of Griffin's tribe, always try to come back and rebuild, so they have to make sure that there won't be any of them left to come in and try again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if some of them were willing, you know, to sit down and have a talk between two different species without it ending in automatic bloodshed, I would be also more than willing to sit down too, listen to their warnings of supernatural evil being a threat to both species, and who knows, maybe I would even invite them to a homemade dinner that is ecologically friendly even according to strictest standards because my rabbits have plenty free space to go around and they eat only natural food. Just let's be good neighbors, though please don't kill those local members of hunter club because I prefer political means of cracking down on them. Probably any reasonable Garou PC would not get an Ally dot because of befriending me, because let's face, I have no political power, but sure, I can donate money to ecological organisation that is front for Garou or sign an initiative.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I should probably make a thread what fun things you would with your Garou friends in spare time that would not be culturally insensitive. </div> </div> </div>7 billion humans. A few tens of thousands of wolves, at the most, and they can be legally hunted and killed in many countries. There's no walking away from the problem for the wolves, because they're slowly being pushed out and killed. There can't be peace, because it far favors the humans. Red Talons killing humans on sight has another practical edge - no human who lives to report the location of their hidden kin can get the news out that there are wolves around, few hunters show up, and the Talons can deal with them far more easily than a huge production. There's no &quot;seeing with eyes unclouded by hate&quot; because the humans are dismissive, and few enough care to really change the opinions of the rest. Hate clouds human eyes far more than those of the Talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-02-2014, 01:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T08:40:20-08:00","id":300023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> One day, you may find that the mask doesn't come off. </div> </div> </div>I might become like my friend June, everyone taking his posts at face value and him ascending to become a living meme.<br /> <br /> Realtalk, I don't deny Red Talon's viewpoint, they are entitled to a one as every being in the universe. I'm only sure if someone threathens one of my values, including my sense of self-preservation, I will fight back, so will Talons. Yes, I can respect that even if I don't agree from subjective viewpoint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-02-2014, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:28:36-08:00","id":300067,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=300008#post300008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">7 billion humans. A few tens of thousands of wolves, at the most, and they can be legally hunted and killed in many countries. There's no walking away from the problem for the wolves, because they're slowly being pushed out and killed. There can't be peace, because it far favors the humans. Red Talons killing humans on sight has another practical edge - no human who lives to report the location of their hidden kin can get the news out that there are wolves around, few hunters show up, and the Talons can deal with them far more easily than a huge production. There's no &quot;seeing with eyes unclouded by hate&quot; because the humans are dismissive, and few enough care to really change the opinions of the rest. Hate clouds human eyes far more than those of the Talons.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I think this applies to any tribe with wolf-kin running free. That's pretty sobering.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T09:38:44-08:00","id":300118,"title":"","content":"I know I talk here about real life, but in defense of my country, many things may be absurd there, but population of wolves is increasing steadily. Would hope there would be more of them since some of weaker carnivores became a pest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T10:51:23-08:00","id":300200,"title":"","content":"The problem is largely an out of character one. Everyone sitting around the table is, obviously, human. some may be higher or lower on the evolutionary slider, but all still human <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And it can be difficult to look at a type of character that regards humans as th ultimate expression of the game's ultimate evil, and <i>not</i> go &quot;well, they're wrong.&quot; While at the same time, it's hard to look at the Walkers, who are almost all human, who have their lupus eating off a plate, and go &quot;they're wrong,&quot; especially as you tap away at your phone and listen to skrillex or whatever.<br /> <br /> You take this perception - that the Red Talons are inherently wrong and evil - and combine it with a general reluctance to play lupus, and another trend that many games seem to have, a focus towards city activities, and we you have a tribe that gets little to no play time, except as rather cartoonish NPC villains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T10:55:05-08:00","id":300203,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299882#post299882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, from what I've seen, the opposite is true. Most PCs even from non-urrah tribes have much more common with the Walkers than Talons.</div> </div> </div> </div>What people play and what the books make available for play are two different things. This statement is true simply by the fact that Homids are the most popular (and populous) Breed and the Red Talons don't have any. The same factors that make playing with cities more popular online is the same reason you see more city viable concepts online. That has nothing to do with why the Red Talons are written up in a problematic way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm just asking in general why they tend to be ignored so much and what could be done to fix the situation for them. Just a curiosity and a thought experiment. And also to consider if I ever put up a game. </div> </div> </div>Redo them completely is my answer. The problem with them is that the only thing that makes the Red Talons distinct from any other Tribe is they take the anti-human bias of the Garou Nation (which yes, should be a thing) to extremes. Almost every Tribe once found it acceptable to cull humans. What would you do with a Red Talon in play back when the culling was still an accepted thing? What would make them special then? Nothing.<br /> <br /> Especially if you find the Red Talon vs. Glasswalker dichotomy interesting, you need to make the Red Talons (1) something that is actually opposite rather than generally so and (2) give them something that doesn't pigeon hole them so strongly away from the other Tribes.<br /> <br /> Solution? Make the Red Talons, essentially, Ratkin (who seem to be pretty popular if you allow Fera in a larger online style game). Make them the Wyld Tribe to the Glasswalker's Weaver Tribe. Their anti-human bias becomes an incidental thing where the humans are just the biggest sources of the Weaver spreading. The death of lots of humans isn't the goal, attacking the Weaver's infrastructures and systems is the goal. That just happens to be really bad for humans on both an immediate level and a social level as chaos and upheaval follows in their wake.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons should love being in the city for the joy of facing their enemies head on. The Wyrm and the Weaver co-mingled in a target rich environment where they can strike both in the name of combating the Wyrm. They can be there to get in the face of all the non-urrah Tribes for getting to cozy with the ways of the city instead of using that knowledge solely to strike at the enemy. Etc. You can even adjust Griffin's ban and have Homid Red Talons but they have to do something like be exposed to the Flux first; to show their dedication to the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Playing a bunch of rabble rousing Wyld proselytes is more appealing than playing a sulky group of assholes trying to prove who hates humans more. And this also changes something pretty important. In the canon cosmology, the Red Talons are basically doing something pointless in the large picture. Yes, avoiding the extinction of wolves is good, but extinctions both happen in nature anyway and its a defensive battle when there's an offensive war to win. Turning them into anti-Weaver extremists means they actually have a point. The Weaver's webs are making the return of the Balance Wyrm impossible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: Though, back to the main question of the thread; Why are the Talons boring, why are the wilds they live in boring? That in itself is part of WtA's world, yet it so easily gets pushed aside in favour of the cities. </div> </div> </div>One, you stated that this is largely coming from a bias of online games. Cities are flat out easier to play in, but we're humans living in them. We understand then and know them. Whereas the number of humans that play online RPGs and are also equally familiar with living out in the true wilderness is a rather small group demographically speaking.<br /> <br /> Cities have a lot of appeal. Most Garou are going to be Homids, which means they are going to grow up in human environments. Two Tribes are heavily linked with urban settings (and two of the bigger ones at that) while one Tribe is explicitly not, and it is supposed to be a very small Tribe for it. Being near an urban area means more enemies to fight, more meaning to the repercussions of the Veil and the Curse, and more for kinfolk if they're being played to do anything. If you're playing in a larger game with interactions between the Garou and Fera, or other supernatural types, the city is the easiest way to facilitated that without it becoming a bloody violence fest.<br /> <br /> That's it in a nutshell. Cities have more options for play than wilderness games. Not that what wilderness games have to offer is bad, just limited to very specific things. There's really no way to escape that without completely redoing WtA.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299915#post299915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The notion that humans are wyrm tainted and should either be exterminated or at best brought back to &quot;controllable&quot; population levels is NOT something that is &quot;exceedingly well represented in the Garou Nation as a whole&quot;. For starters, all the other Tribes have homid Kinfolk (usually more than lupus). This means a Get lupus CANNOT hold this position at all, since it basically means he wants to kill over half of his own Kinfolk, which would be.....odd at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>The notion that humans are out of control is well represented as a position amongst the Garou. As I said, what makes the Red Talons different is that they're extremists about it. They're willing to play the, &quot;I hate humans more than you!&quot; game, instead of accepting that humans exist, the Litany in fact demands that you can't just eradicate them, and actually doing something more useful than turning themselves into outcasts since, as you point out, the other Tribes don't like the idea that the Red Talons want their families dead.<br /> <br /> My point is not that a Lupus Fenrir is the same as a Red Talon, but they can fill the narrative role of &quot;big bad wolf that despises humanity&quot; just fine. They're not the same because they're just going to go kill the Wyrm instead of becoming anti-human extremists. Even if they fundamentally agree on the position the Red Talons are starting on.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T12:20:25-08:00","id":300263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=300203#post300203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One, you stated that this is largely coming from a bias of online games. Cities are flat out easier to play in, but we're humans living in them. We understand then and know them. Whereas the number of humans that play online RPGs and are also equally familiar with living out in the true wilderness is a rather small group demographically speaking.<br /> <br /> Cities have a lot of appeal. Most Garou are going to be Homids, which means they are going to grow up in human environments. Two Tribes are heavily linked with urban settings (and two of the bigger ones at that) while one Tribe is explicitly not, and it is supposed to be a very small Tribe for it. Being near an urban area means more enemies to fight, more meaning to the repercussions of the Veil and the Curse, and more for kinfolk if they're being played to do anything. If you're playing in a larger game with interactions between the Garou and Fera, or other supernatural types, the city is the easiest way to facilitated that without it becoming a bloody violence fest.<br /> <br /> That's it in a nutshell. Cities have more options for play than wilderness games. Not that what wilderness games have to offer is bad, just limited to very specific things. There's really no way to escape that without completely redoing WtA.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, there is more to do in cities. Though, I've seen the problem between rural caern VS city solved by having a city board on the forum for city focused characters. So it's not impossible to combine them.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm looking for is, how to drum up interest in a rural sept game as a concept. And through that, see the viability of Talons.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T13:28:42-08:00","id":300364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, there is more to do in cities. Though, I've seen the problem between rural caern VS city solved by having a city board on the forum for city focused characters. So it's not impossible to combine them.<br /> <br /> I guess what I'm looking for is, how to drum up interest in a rural sept game as a concept. And through that, see the viability of Talons. </div> </div> </div>Only way I could encourage one of my players to play in rural setting would be if he could play a redneck. Whelp, Hillfolk of Bone Gnawers are kind of 'rednecks' <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But realtalk, rural settings can be charming and they have their own merits, that said by someone who lives on the edge of a small town and can visit all those villages on foot. Small town setting like that could be a wonderful compromise, though I doubt there is much Wyrm-taint in my town. Any threat like that would have to come from outside. And there is a good place for a caern in one of villages, which happens to be next to a place where we keep European bisons under protection. Probably Silver Fang dominated Sept, due to various reasons.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T16:38:15-08:00","id":300535,"title":"","content":"I think the Red Talons are fine as they are. They are often limited as a PC choice because 1) most players prefer to play homids, 2) a lot of games aren't based in areas where there is large wilderness, and 3) many STs don't know how to run a game where lupus issues are prominent. That's not the fault of the Tribe. I think it's good they exist for those troupes who do see a use for them. I think online games are more limiting because the nature of the play are more limiting to lupus.<br /> <br /> Portrayal in WoD materials may need to better, but honestly I find that is the case with many tribes, clans, traditions, etc. Generally I find the core books to be filled with very strong images and themes that are badly developed in subsequent books. I usually keep the things I like, jettison those I don't, and introduce my own ideas.<br /> <br /> In general, I tend to run focused games in Werewolf with limited options for tribes appropriate to the setting I have. I did run a brief campaign where Red Talons were an option and prepared a lot of materials to help players. Those who played Talons had a blast. We explored lots of different things involving the Wyrm that did not involve humanity necessarily which pointed the tribe's ire in a different direction, and I had a plot with humans reintroducing wolves into the wilderness (which is why the Tribe sent some Cliaths down to that area) which caused some good character interaction.<br /> <br /> Even if not as PCs, I think a good ST can do lots of fun stuff with the tribe as NPCs. They are actually one of my favorite tribes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T11:32:54-08:00","id":301368,"title":"","content":"Black Fox, I'd love to see some plot summaries of those games! Having solid ideas of Red Talon stuff to run would be real nice.<br /> <br /> For me I think one reason people have problems with Talons is, they don't logically fit into any campaign that isn't focused around them. They're not short on plot points, it's just that their plots are generally mutually exclusive, it's like running a game with both vampire and garou PCs--even if you give them a common foe, it's not going to last, and they aren't going to be in the same place at the same time anyway. Run a one-off game with a mostly- or all-Talon pack, something where you see them as more than strawmen, and they'll feel a lot more developed after that.<br /> <br /> Also, the lupus form is _hard_ to run tabletop or LARP. You can't really appreciate or convey the differences in communication of being in that form for a long time as easily. Forums or MUSHes are easier that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2214-traveller","name":"Traveller","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2214_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-03T21:36:22-08:00","id":301803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Traveller</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=301368#post301368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Fox, I'd love to see some plot summaries of those games! Having solid ideas of Red Talon stuff to run would be real nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been over ten years so I don't have summaries easily available. But here are some things I remember.<br /> <br /> 1) Make individual animals distinctive NPCs. Determine who are the key species, and have at least one member of each detailed in appearance and personality. Any names will be those your Talon (or lupus or even general Garou) NPCs gave them. Read Bambi by Felix Salten - lots of ideas on how to portray animals. Jungle Book is also awesome. Aesops Fables is also helpful. For more contemporary, something like Mouse Guard is even good. Watership Down and Plague Dogs as well. Detail your wolves and wolf kinfolk a lot, but don't neglect your rival predators and prey (big and small - deer, beaver, mouse, squirrel) and the distinction between wild, tamed, and domesticated animals.<br /> <br /> 2) Emphasis on spirits interaction in the Umbra is essential. Talons are basically there to help regulate that. Are wolves not finding enough prey? Find out why the spirits of the prey animals are offended. Even outside of wolves, Talon Theurges can be kept busy mediating disputes between rival spirits flocks; or trying to get rain or weather spirits to work as they should especially if weather is erratic - drought, floods, or such.<br /> <br /> 3) Natural disasters can lead to a lot of cool scenes, especially once PC Talons accept other animals as real NPCs they care about or dislike. Set a massive wildfire in the woods and you'll have plenty of drama.<br /> <br /> 4) I highlighted that the purpose of predators are to cull the weak and sick, not the strong. Same applies to humans. You can teach Talons to be selective of what kind of humans they should kill and get good discussions on what is definition of weak and sick as it relates to humans.<br /> <br /> 5) The Talons in my chronicle had to deal with the fact the reintroduction of wolves in the area were the result of humans; and that evidence of wolves hurting humans and livestock would endanger the wolves. This forced the Talons to develop a strategy on what they could or could not do, especially since there were a few other tribes in the chronicle as well.<br /> <br /> 6) Have the Talons deal with threats from invasive species - plants, vermin, animals, whatever.<br /> <br /> 7) Be more creative with Wyrm creatures. Less Fomori or man made toxic spells, and more ancient horrors hidden in the Earth or coming from the outer dark. I go all Lovecraftian - I have them deal with Colors out of Space, Fire Vampires, Shoggoths, or whatever. Have Banes be disease spirits infecting your prey animals or whatever. Show how the Wyrm manifests outside of Man. Be creative with your Wyrm creatures to focus the game away from &quot;killing humans.&quot;<br /> <br /> 8) Use the deep wilderness as a benefit. Keep small human settlements. Have areas of the forest or prairie or whatever where people don't visit so that it belongs only to the animals and Garou.<br /> <br /> It is a very different game than most people are used to, but it can be very fun if you have the right players. The Talons are the only tribe not dominated by homids. Even though other tribes have lupus, those lupus are a distinct minority and don't set the agenda of the tribe. As a result, a Talons chronicle can highlight a lot of things homids don't think are important, but actually are to the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-06T04:45:30-08:00","id":304446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 6) Have the Talons deal with threats from invasive species - plants, vermin, animals, whatever. </div> </div> </div>I suggest feral 'house&quot; cats. They may be second most proficient species at killing off whole species. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T02:31:51-08:00","id":307280,"title":"","content":"Cats are easy for Talons to deal with; hunt 'em down, eat 'em.<br /> <br /> Kudzu, though? Short of burning it or eating it, it's almost uncontrollable (and burning it is a temporary fix)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/612-the-cat-came-back","name":"The Cat Came Back","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar612_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"243"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T03:30:10-08:00","id":307295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cats are easy for Talons to deal with; hunt 'em down, eat 'em. </div> </div> </div>Unless Pentex gives them a boost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-09T20:24:09-08:00","id":307817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Cat Came Back</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=307280#post307280\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cats are easy for Talons to deal with; hunt 'em down, eat 'em.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Red Talons in North America wouldn't need to. The coyotes in the area would take care of that for them. Their dilemma would likely involve support of the coyotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T01:49:12-08:00","id":307987,"title":"","content":"Another problem is that feral cats breed so damn fast that it may require institutional solutions too. The plan:<br /> <br /> 1. City based Tribes lobby for action of neutering stray cats.<br /> <br /> 2. Red Talons and other Tribes accustomed to the wild are responsible for the culling part of those which slip under the radar<br /> <br /> Surely cats are menace to treat seriously. Dwarf Fortress taught me so.<br /> <br /> In my country it's fox problem. Not enough cats actually, and we suffer from that because rodents get bold again. Meantime wild birds and small mammals that live in the wild get decimated by out of control fox population. Even if we have enough wolves, as I read, to 'export' them to Germany (healthy response, humans ditch my beautiful country too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-10T06:27:52-08:00","id":308157,"title":"","content":"The Red Talons are perhaps the smallest Tribe of the Garou Nation and the reason they are so often limited in things like Online venues is because of that whole Anti-Human stance and the problem of dealing with the Urban world that doesn't threaten Frenzy tests. <br /> <br /> They should totally be a voice in the Nation when presented in a Tabletop game, but they are a fading failing voice due to the kinfolk dying out etc. But they are not a dead voice and they should really be why places that are Wild are still feared by man in the World of Darkness. The problem is that too many people see RedTalon and go &quot;Rarrrg Kill Monkies&quot;. See that's wrong, because the Talon's are intelligent, they're not Human educated by they are Garou educated. They place a greater value on instinct but Wolves are really clever predators and Garou leave wolves standing. Thing is the Talon's HATE humanity and it's justified, but they're not unthinking creatures fuelled just by Rage (well some of the Ahrouns might be, but that's the same across the board). The Talons hold firmly to the line of the Wild and think nothing of slaughtering any human they find outside the safety of their cities, they want Mankind to be afraid of the Wild places, of the dark of night, of the howl on the wind and they can certainly reason as well as any Glasswalker or Shadowlord into making those things happen. The RedTalons are very much all the terrifying parts that fill the human psyche on Monster Stories or classical werewolf tales and movies but amplified by the fact that they are totally sentient creatures.<br /> <br /> For those who find the Wild places &quot;boring&quot; or &quot;lacking focus&quot; I well recommend the Book of the Wyld and the Monster segments of the Book of the Wyrm 2nd edit (I dare say Wyrm20 will also have really handy stuff). Also Rage Across the Heavens and Book of the Umbra, because these are All places where the RedTalons are just as at home as any other Garou and in some places even more so (obviously umbral realms will vary) and with the exception of a few Umbral Realms are all well outside any of the concepts of the City. Also take a peek at the Werewolf Dark Ages books as they deal with a lot of wild too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T19:33:28-08:00","id":309745,"title":"","content":"To be perfectly simple and honest, I don't like the Red Talons because their entire worldview has always struck me as not very Gaian and dangerously Wyrmy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u200b<span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\">Dante \u201cOwns-All-the-Books\u201d Laughing-Coyote<br /> <a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/91390940/Werewolf%20the%20Apocalypse%20Reference.xlsx\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf (and Human) Reference Excel Spreadsheet</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/clouddrive/share?s=VoD6R2UDSGwijaft3H4kbM\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img593/9752/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img546/6111/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1765-rderekp","name":"rderekp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1765_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-11T20:50:40-08:00","id":309844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>rderekp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=309745#post309745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be perfectly simple and honest, I don't like the Red Talons because their entire worldview has always struck me as not very Gaian and dangerously Wyrmy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just 'cause some werewolves want to kill all humans, that makes them radicals?<br /> <br /> [/Werewolf Bender]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T07:04:06-08:00","id":310216,"title":"","content":"In all honesty it's a rather Wyrmy world view but entirely applicable in the original sense of the 'Wyrm'. The Impergium went too far but it was only at that point the Celestines stepped in, the early years of the Impergium was fine (infact it's exactly the thing the Ratkin exist for). Also the Tribe view of the RedTalons isn't just &quot;Kill all humans&quot;, they are equally deep preservers of the wilderness and champions of the Wyld, they are the most primeval of mystics and deeply in tune with the instinctual rhythms of existence. As a tribe they're also isolationists, not always the best option for a character to massively embrace but can add a ton of mystique as NPCs or a plot point in a campaign. Thing is we make them one dimensional by only focussing on the anti human thing.<br /> <br /> Something I do when introducing new people to WTA or giving novice players a look on tribes they haven't really looked at is by attaching not one but three &quot;Descriptors&quot; about the generic tribe overview. For example...<br /> <br /> Black Furies: &quot;Amazon Heroines&quot; &quot;Wise Women &amp; Seers&quot; &quot;Den Mothers, Pack Sisters, Protectors of the Family&quot; <br /> Fianna: &quot;Fury of Legend&quot; &quot;Songs &amp; Howls of the Ancients&quot; &quot;Mysterious Magic&quot; <br /> Bone Gnawers: &quot;Tenacious Warriors&quot; &quot;Streetwise Infiltrators&quot; &quot;Pragamtic Idealists&quot;<br /> <br /> For RedTalons I go with<br /> &quot;Embittered Survivors&quot; &quot;Defenders of the 'Lost, Forgotten and Unseen' world&quot; &quot;Primeval Mystics&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T07:56:09-08:00","id":310248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=310216#post310216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In all honesty it's a rather Wyrmy world view but entirely applicable in the original sense of the 'Wyrm'. The Impergium went too far but it was only at that point the Celestines stepped in,</div> </div> </div> </div>The Celestines never stepped in. This was an affair entirely with the Changers, none of whom fell to the Wyrm for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T08:36:01-08:00","id":310266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=310216#post310216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is we make them one dimensional by only focussing on the anti human thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we can call this a particularly fan-faulted thing. The W20 core book spends a huge amount of the Red Talon word count on their anti-humanity thing, and almost nothing on the more compelling aspects of the Tribe beyond that. Someone reading the core book and your three descriptive phrases about the Red Talons is most likely to just be confused as hell. Especially as nothing in your descriptors includes their anti-humanity sentiment directly while the book stresses it repeatedly, and nothing really supports them as &quot;Primeval Mystics&quot; outside of having Theurges. Their Gifts List, for example, doesn't have any particular emphasis on mystic issues. Most of their Gifts are more about being better hunters via tracking, stealth, and mental harassment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T09:07:29-08:00","id":310281,"title":"","content":"I agree entirely Heavy Arms on the way much of the material shows us the AntiHuman thing and I agree to a point with the Gifts comment. <br /> <br /> But I'm speaking and assessing from a long experience within the WTA mythos (one that you have as well, as do several posters) and am drawing my conclusions from things like Book of the Wyld, Rage Across the Heavens, references in Axis Mundi correlating with Griffons Brood, appropriate Realm segments from book of the Umbra, information suggested in the Players Guide to Garou and the Storytellers Guide. My descriptors I use for the tribes I try to avoid the most &quot;in your face&quot; thing you get from the quick blurb in the book, but I try to reference it. That's why I don't reference Feminism or AntiMale for the Furies, I don't use the Underdog or Omega scuzzy aspect for the BoneGnawers etc, I also expect that other STs of varying experience may use different descriptors. I find them helpful to use to get my players thinking about their character within their tribe in multiple dimensions (they also help me pull together random Garou npc's at a glance). Which spurs me to this... What three Descriptors would you (the collective you of the Forum users, not just Heavy Arms) use to describe the RedTalons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T10:07:13-08:00","id":310368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=310281#post310281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which spurs me to this... What three Descriptors would you (the collective you of the Forum users, not just Heavy Arms) use to describe the RedTalons?</div> </div> </div> </div>Here goes;<br /> <br /> Uncomplicated- To a Red Talon, a lot of things are simple. A garou needs a pack, a garou needs to do their auspice duty, fight the Wyrm and protect the Caern. And they do not complicate things with over-thinking, if you need to pack you will pack regardless of your personal opinion. If you need to protect a Caern, you will do so, even if it means dying.<br /> <br /> Voice of the Wilderness- Not Wyld, for Wyld is not nature same way Weaver is not the city. Red Talons are creatures of the animal kingdom, as Black Fox suggested above. This means they often voice not just their own opinions, but the opinions of the prey and the land itself.<br /> <br /> Unchanging- I always like to point out the bad side of a tribe, and beyond the human-killing, I think this is the Red Talons' worst aspect. They hate the Weaver and the way cities are with humans. Glass Walkers are their opposite and so they are viewned in a bad light. But, yet, Walkers adapt and change, Talons have stuck to the same way for centuries. Nature is never static, it is never unchanging, yet the Talons stick to their ways none the less. Is this a good thing? Or is a flaw?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T17:28:08-08:00","id":310747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just 'cause some werewolves want to kill all humans, that makes them radicals? </div> </div> </div>From perspective of humans, yes. From their own perspective, that's not.<br /> <br /> Though I wonder how that Red Talon antagonist I had in mind would be radical from perspective of the Tribe if he wanted to keep minority of humans left to &quot;redo&quot;. The tiny minority who would survive his scheme would be maybe worth enough to this time &quot;remake&quot; humans to be more Gaian aligned.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-12-2014, 08:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T21:41:41-08:00","id":310900,"title":"","content":"Just a reminder that it is the Lodge of the Predator Kings which is the camp who wants to exterminate mankind. That is one camp; and they are obviously meant as antagonists. The majority of the tribe, the Warders of the Land, won't hesitate to kill a human who is a threat, but don't intend to fight a war against humanity or kill everyone. Then of course the so-called Whelp's Compromise actually believe there is some purpose or value to mankind, otherwise why would Gaia have made them? The idea that Red Talons all want to kill humans is no more accurate than stating all Black Furies are lesbian man-killers. Those are very obvious hooks, and it is not a surprise many STs and Players grab onto that first either as a stereotype or how they introduce the first NPC of the tribe, but it doesn't accurately describe the tribe.<br /> <br /> If anything, the primary emotion of the Red Talons towards Man is not hatred, but fear. They don't understand humanity, and don't understand how after 10,000 years of small numbers clad in leather using bone weapons, humanity has become this huge threat with metal claws and stings possessing cities and huge numbers in only two to four thousand years.<br /> <br /> I think there is a lot to explore with the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T12:55:09-08:00","id":311566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=299915#post299915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That is....not my experience, to put it mildly. And I've played a few Talons, also used them as NPCs a lot.<br /> <br /> The notion that humans are wyrm tainted and should either be exterminated or at best brought back to &quot;controllable&quot; population levels is NOT something that is &quot;exceedingly well represented in the Garou Nation as a whole&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I respectfully disagree:<br /> <br /> &quot;...Because we need humans and wolves to pass on our line, we have to protect humanity and wolves alike for our own good as well as theirs. And believe me, if it weren't for that, humanity might have died out long ago. There are too many of us who see humans as the enemy.&quot; (Page 7. Werewolf).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/19/w20supporterheavymetal1.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/545/7z8m.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/829/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3506-uniform-two-six","name":"Uniform Two Six","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3506_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T13:28:43-08:00","id":312506,"title":"","content":"I disagree that Red Talons have no place in a city game, though it is true that it puts you in a situation of many many rage checks. As an ST - I usually involve a lot of rage checks in my game, which balances it out. I don't like it when my players forget that they are, in fact, biting back at the urge to go full spree killer on their home town. However - to the point:<br /> <br /> Search some of the popular World of Darkness locations on Google Maps. (Los Angeles, Seattle, etc.) Being from the east coast of the US, I'm used to a very crowded human world. Out in the American West, though... once you leave those city borders, it's not very far before you find there's a whole lot of nothing. Even Los Angeles can look like a pretty small bastion of safety in the dark wilderness that borders it. In my games Red Talons are the reason why city people look out into the dark wilderness with a shiver of fear. They are the alpha predators. They howl and bark at the edges of humanity, and still inspire the primordial fear that the delirium represents. If you're looking for a few examples of how you can use them in games without having to fall to the old &quot;kill all humans&quot; stereotype, I can offer a few of mine to ponder as you please.<br /> <br /> First, I often use them in tangent with the Ratkin. As a previous poster mentioned, Gaia specifically created the ratkin to cull humanity. The Garou kind of just helped. In this set up, the Ratkin usually handle the inner city work and inform the Red Talons of high value human targets leaving their domain. If you like to play more hateful with your fera, the corax are usually more than happy to facilitate these sorts of collaborations (for suitable pay).<br /> <br /> My Red Talon NPC, which I left open as a mentor for anyone who felt up to the task of going full Lupus, was named Prowls-the-Starless-Night. He was the Keeper of the Land for the local Sept, and had a habit of mercilessly tearing apart anything that upset his balance... or anyone who questioned his method. Just the same though, we're talking a Warder here. Not interested in the fire and death approach to culling humanity. I don't think a Get can play the big bad wolf like a Red Talon can. Get are warriors and perfect the art of battle. Red Talons are predators, and perfect the art of being more cunning, more stealthy and all-together more terrifying.<br /> <br /> If you're looking at Red Talons from a human perspective, you should be affraid of them just deciding you need to die today. If you want a loyal friend - go find a Bone Gnawer. These are Red Talons, they're only interested in the Darwin-esque laws of nature.<br /> <br /> Some of these thoughts are only half formed. Sorry, I'm in a rush to finish this post and get out the door. I hope some of this was interesting to think about.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-14T21:41:27-08:00","id":312762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=312506#post312506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">.<br /> <br /> If you're looking at Red Talons from a human perspective, you should be affraid of them just deciding you need to die today. If you want a loyal friend - go find a Bone Gnawer. These are Red Talons, they're only interested in the <u>Darwin-esque laws of nature</u>.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Alright, you miserable apes - we're going to see how many children you have and what traits they carry. Based on that, you miserable offences to Gaia will know who has more children surviving to breeding age!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...There's not much more to add, honestly. Que sera, sera.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:13:07-08:00","id":313293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=312762#post312762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Alright, you miserable apes - we're going to see how many children you have and what traits they carry. Based on that, you miserable offences to Gaia will know who has more children surviving to breeding age!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...There's not much more to add, honestly. Que sera, sera.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And that's why they aren't popular. I mean we can talk all SimWOd all we want but its hard enough to play an animal changer much less ones that are notoriously antihuman. I mean just being &quot;antihuman&quot; is generally enough to be an evil race in most fantasy settings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T14:32:17-08:00","id":313302,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313293#post313293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And that's why they aren't popular. I mean we can talk all SimWOd all we want but its hard enough to play an animal changer much less ones that are notoriously antihuman. I mean just being &quot;antihuman&quot; is generally enough to be an evil race in most fantasy settings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I was riffing off the other poster's use of &quot;Darwin-esque rules of nature&quot; there. It was a joke, but I'm also tired.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T19:03:05-08:00","id":313405,"title":"","content":"I would like to point out vis-a-vis the &quot;Evil&quot; thing. Werewolf is meant to be a game of Savage Horror, you ARE playing a Monster, a terrible monster that can reduce a bar full of people into a web sticky mess because someone spilled your pint. You scare people just by walking down the street and they don't even know why. You'll butcher people who are in the wrong place at the wrong time, because while humanity matter they don't matter &quot;That Much&quot;. That's the truth of it for all Garou, even the ones who care, because the War and the Apocalypse are far far more important. Rage is far more powerful than simple good intentions. <br /> <br /> Sure, you're a Hero, but only to the Garou and the cause they fight for. Some poor guy gets a bane in him through a bad batch of King Beer and it starts causing other banes to spawn. You can't cleanse him, you can't save him, you have to kill him it's the only way to make the bane vulnerable. The Litany is upheld, a threat to Gaia is removed, your deeds spread through the Nation, and you just killed A Guy. The RedTalons are just seeing a deeper corruption and the terrifying thing is, they are not really wrong. The rest of the Nation isn't protecting humanity, they're just trying to circumvent the threat that Mankind can pose to the efforts of the War and directly to the Tribes. The Talons certainly want to go too far and are almost vindictive in their desires, but they remind the other Garou that really and truly humanity do need to be bled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-15T21:33:26-08:00","id":313485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313405#post313405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to point out vis-a-vis the &quot;Evil&quot; thing. Werewolf is meant to be a game of Savage Horror, you ARE playing a Monster, a terrible monster that can reduce a bar full of people into a web sticky mess because someone spilled your pint. You scare people just by walking down the street and they don't even know why. You'll butcher people who are in the wrong place at the wrong time, because while humanity matter they don't matter &quot;That Much&quot;. That's the truth of it for all Garou, even the ones who care, because the War and the Apocalypse are far far more important. Rage is far more powerful than simple good intentions.<br /> <br /> Sure, you're a Hero, but only to the Garou and the cause they fight for. Some poor guy gets a bane in him through a bad batch of King Beer and it starts causing other banes to spawn. You can't cleanse him, you can't save him, you have to kill him it's the only way to make the bane vulnerable. The Litany is upheld, a threat to Gaia is removed, your deeds spread through the Nation, and you just killed A Guy. The RedTalons are just seeing a deeper corruption and the terrifying thing is, they are not really wrong. The rest of the Nation isn't protecting humanity, they're just trying to circumvent the threat that Mankind can pose to the efforts of the War and directly to the Tribes. The Talons certainly want to go too far and are almost vindictive in their desires, but they remind the other Garou that really and truly humanity do need to be bled.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You are missing my point by falling into the whole SimWOD view. You are trying to defend them from an In universe point of view. The thing is their distinct lack of popularity has nothing whatsoever to do with whether they are in universe right. They are Alien to the player, they hate everything the player knows and loves. Its hard to get into the role, its hard to sell people on &quot;everything you do sucks&quot; and they don't even get to be the &quot;Evil' splat, so you don't get the &quot;I want play evil&quot; players to cover their basis. They require signficant buy into the game setup to enjoy, and thus will never be popular.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T03:12:52-08:00","id":313590,"title":"","content":"Not so much, Lian. The entire reason the World of Darkness did so well to begin with was because you got to play a Monster. It was at it's time unique in this and most of the things around then didn't really have the same moral granularity (they could but it wasn't a solid default) with things like Cyberpunk and Shadowrun coming close but even with them it was expressing how your character wasn't a monster of some sort. It's not an In Universe view at all, it's a core game premise for a game of Savage Horror. That the Talons require a &quot;buy in&quot; to be played is a solid reflection on that. A great many of the Tribes require a Buy In to be effective in their flavour and almost every character requires it too, this is why I like to play with the optional Tribal Flaws at times. I'm a massive SilverFang fan and every last one of them that I have played has been Mad to one level or another and in every case it's been a very carefully chosen and represented madness, by rights people shouldn't enjoy playing any mad character because that is alien to them but they seem popular enough. Handling Rage right out the gate by the same logic should make Werewolves unpopular to play, remember that anything that might make a normal person angry or annoyed or shout or swear might make a Garou frenzy and rip things into pieces. <br /> <br /> There are plenty of people out there who enjoy all these aspects of the game and there are plenty who enjoy the RedTalons? Why? Because it presents a challenge, it presents a need to do something else and really think about character actions and how they differ from your own. It's a reason to understand things that would not otherwise enter your mind and to express that in a storytelling medium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T08:02:04-08:00","id":313684,"title":"","content":"NB: Silver Fang derangements are purely optional, as were any other Tribal Weaknesses (and their lack of popularity is why they aren't reproduced in W20).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T09:33:54-08:00","id":313782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313485#post313485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You are missing my point by falling into the whole SimWOD view. You are trying to defend them from an In universe point of view. The thing is their distinct lack of popularity has nothing whatsoever to do with whether they are in universe right. They are Alien to the player, they hate everything the player knows and loves. Its hard to get into the role, its hard to sell people on &quot;everything you do sucks&quot; and they don't even get to be the &quot;Evil' splat, so you don't get the &quot;I want play evil&quot; players to cover their basis. They require signficant buy into the game setup to enjoy, and thus will never be popular.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd not say they are that alien to the player. As Moirdryd allready noted, WoD is based on playing the monster. But there is another reason why Talons wouldn't be that alien. Aside from the setting, a lot of people who are aware of the state of the enviroment can understand the reactions and anger. You may live a life of modern devices, but you can also know the price of it. And exploring that side, the inhumanity of nature striking back, is one reason why people might want to play Talons.<br /> <br /> It's also a core theme of WtA, that humanity isn't all there is. That is why we have the feral breeds, to balance the human aspect out. And while they can be played poorly, often they can also be rewarding to play and see the world through the eyes of a non-human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T10:53:24-08:00","id":313844,"title":"","content":"I said the flaws were optional and, on that note, they didn't appear in core WTAr or 2nd either. <br /> The RedTalons represent an important dynamic in the Garou and one that it's a solid option for people to explore. We see plenty of people going &quot;BSD Game!&quot; surely if anything should be Alien it should be the Labyrinth maddened, insane and twisted fallen tribe of the Garou, but for some reason lots of people don't think it is. That in and of itself should maybe give us pause and grant some insight into the position of the RedTalons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T11:32:49-08:00","id":313864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313844#post313844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said the flaws were optional and, on that note, they didn't appear in core WTAr or 2nd either.<br /> The RedTalons represent an important dynamic in the Garou and one that it's a solid option for people to explore. We see plenty of people going &quot;BSD Game!&quot; surely if anything should be Alien it should be the Labyrinth maddened, insane and twisted fallen tribe of the Garou, but for some reason lots of people don't think it is. That in and of itself should maybe give us pause and grant some insight into the position of the RedTalons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's because, as with all tribes other than Talons, people just go with homid or very homid-like metis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T11:34:39-08:00","id":313866,"title":"","content":"I still don't think a solid case has been made for the Red Talons, as written in the books, represent an important dynamic. I don't think there's a significant case for, &quot;lupus angry at humans without having to deal with Homids in their own Tribe,&quot; as doing anything. There's nothing in this thread at all that shows the Red Talons as written have a dynamic that actually needs this set up.<br /> <br /> If I want a lupus that's rightfully pissed off at humanity and doesn't balk at killing humans that despoil the few remaining wilds, and is focused on those wilderness areas... I can pretty much do that with any tribe besides the Glasswalkers. The dynamic of them having to deal with the more homid-centric Garou Nation is a more direct issue when they have Tribemates to deal with that are homids.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T11:44:55-08:00","id":313871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313866#post313866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't think a solid case has been made for the Red Talons, as written in the books, represent an important dynamic. I don't think there's a significant case for, &quot;lupus angry at humans without having to deal with Homids in their own Tribe,&quot; as doing anything. There's nothing in this thread at all that shows the Red Talons as written have a dynamic that actually needs this set up.<br /> <br /> If I want a lupus that's rightfully pissed off at humanity and doesn't balk at killing humans that despoil the few remaining wilds, and is focused on those wilderness areas... I can pretty much do that with any tribe besides the Glasswalkers. The dynamic of them having to deal with the more homid-centric Garou Nation is a more direct issue when they have Tribemates to deal with that are homids.</div> </div> </div> </div>Such isolation of like minds is liable to give rise to its own culture. One way or another, Red Talons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T12:49:49-08:00","id":313912,"title":"","content":"A cross Tribal Camp of lupus is a very different cultural point than a Tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T13:10:54-08:00","id":313917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313590#post313590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not so much, Lian. The entire reason the World of Darkness did so well to begin with was because you got to play a Monster. It was at it's time unique in this and most of the things around then didn't really have the same moral granularity (they could but it wasn't a solid default) with things like Cyberpunk and Shadowrun coming close but even with them it was expressing how your character wasn't a monster of some sort.</div> </div> </div> </div>And you don't see how that's equally reflected in WOD? Masquerade litterally has a stat saying &quot;I'm not a horrible person&quot;. Werewolf isn't about being an uncontrollable killing machine all the time its about war with the wyrm. There's alot of grey but its pretty damned clear that the argument is being made that &quot;you aren't a monster because..&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not an In Universe view at all, it's a core game premise for a game of Savage Horror. That the Talons require a &quot;buy in&quot; to be played is a solid reflection on that. A great many of the Tribes require a Buy In to be effective in their flavour and almost every character requires it too, </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure Glasswalker homid hacker requires signficantly less buy in than any Red Talon and I will bet real money is a much more commonly played character than Red Talons in general.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> this is why I like to play with the optional Tribal Flaws at times. I'm a massive SilverFang fan and every last one of them that I have played has been Mad to one level or another and in every case it's been a very carefully chosen and represented madness, by rights people shouldn't enjoy playing any mad character because that is alien to them but they seem popular enough. Handling Rage right out the gate by the same logic should make Werewolves unpopular to play, remember that anything that might make a normal person angry or annoyed or shout or swear might make a Garou frenzy and rip things into pieces. </div> </div> </div><br /> Notice how these are optional? do you think the majority of people use it? Also I know people who have OCD, Depression all sorts of mental ailments. I've never met however a person who was born a wolf suddenly gained sapience after a year of life and generally hates everything about me. Every form of Madness is more relateable than a Red Talon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are plenty of people out there who enjoy all these aspects of the game and there are plenty who enjoy the RedTalons? Why? Because it presents a challenge, it presents a need to do something else and really think about character actions and how they differ from your own. It's a reason to understand things that would not otherwise enter your mind and to express that in a storytelling medium. </div> </div> </div>Yes. I'm not saying Red Talons don't have fans. I'm not saying they don't serve a purpose. I am saying Red Talons are Werewolf &quot;hard mode&quot;. They have a completely Alien mind set, not just alien though but fairly uncomfortable. Its hard to say &quot;humans aren't important&quot;(and those are the nice Talons) or that all humans need to die. On a very basic level people believe we are important, people believe human life matters. Its almost a visceral feeling, so its very hard to get into the Lupus much less Red Talon mindset. I'm not saying they need to be gotten rid of because of this(This isn't Games workshop!), but that being hard to play, or portray well makes them tend to be rarely used.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313844#post313844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I said the flaws were optional and, on that note, they didn't appear in core WTAr or 2nd either.<br /> The RedTalons represent an important dynamic in the Garou and one that it's a solid option for people to explore. We see plenty of people going &quot;BSD Game!&quot; surely if anything should be Alien it should be the Labyrinth maddened, insane and twisted fallen tribe of the Garou, but for some reason lots of people don't think it is. That in and of itself should maybe give us pause and grant some insight into the position of the RedTalons.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's always been people who want to play unredeemable evil. To go around murdering people &quot;For the Lolz&quot; There's always been people complaining about humanity, about the Litany, about Avatars pushing to Ascension when they want to play without any real consequences. They want to play Grand theft werewolf.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure if this group is larger than those who want to play werewolf hardmode. However werewolf hardmode is actively supported by the books(Way of the Wolf, Changing Ways) while playing a BSD isn't so people are going to probably speak up more about how awesome they are for sticking it to the Man and playing BSDs or How they need help doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2715,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","user":"Lian","date":". 11-16-2014, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T13:11:15-08:00","id":313918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313912#post313912\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A cross Tribal Camp of lupus is a very different cultural point than a Tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there's liable to be a big enough spirit that hates humans to act as a totem. From Camp to Tribe!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T13:44:00-08:00","id":313934,"title":"","content":"But that just returns to what's so lacking in the Red Talons. Being defined solely by, &quot;we hate humans more than everyone else,&quot; is simply too little to hang meaningfully interesting characters off of as a core Tribe. Everything that tries to expand on them more ends up either failing to do so because &quot;we hate humans more&quot; is still the core point, or ends up muddled and undifferentiated from lupus in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T14:04:04-08:00","id":313943,"title":"","content":"Thing is, Heavy Arms, exactly the same applies to all the Tribes. Why is there a tribe of Kings? Of Shady power hungry manipulators? Of street born guttersnipes? Of weaver linked city wolves? Of angry natives? Of mystical natives? Of Song and mythology? Or Warriors? Of female warriors? Of medative martial artists? I can do any of those with any other tribe. The entire point of the Splats in WoD is to represent parts of the Mythos from which the game line is inspired and buildt around. Each Camarilla clan represents an aspect of the Camarilla concept of &quot;Vampire&quot; and each Werewolf Tribe gives an identity to an aspect of the Garou. <br /> The Silverfangs the Alpha concept, the leading hero, the failing fight with a glimmer of hope. <br /> The Shadowlords Do what Must be Done and exert strength and power and beware the cost. <br /> The Fianna are the Songs and Tales that build Legends and a connection to Otherworlds<br /> The Black Furies are the nurturing she wolf and protection of the pack with ancient wisdom and fury<br /> The Uktena are the dark secrets of the world and the unseen sacrifice made to keep the Wyrm at bay<br /> The Wendigo are the tribal history of Man and the distrust of any Not Garou<br /> The Glasswalkers are the Wolf in Sheeps clothing<br /> The BoneGnawers are the Omega and the underdog fighting against bad odds<br /> The Stargazers are the disconnect of knowing truths the rest of the world will never see<br /> The Red Talons are the Wild and Primal Rage of the Werewolf, unleashed and untamed<br /> The Children of Gaia are the balancing act within every Garou<br /> The Get of Fenris are the relentless warriors ready to face any foe.<br /> The Croatan are the ultimate sacrifice, the line in the sand<br /> The WhiteHowlers the empty sacrifice born of being the Lone Wolf or Hubris<br /> The Black Spiral Dancers the failure and surrender and the traitors. <br /> The Bunyip are the way that a Werewolf is different from those they may share much with (and the results of their own prejudices ). <br /> The Siberakh are a hope based in prophecies but also the ultimate isolation of the Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2767,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","user":"Moirdryd","date":". 11-16-2014, 05:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T14:57:35-08:00","id":313988,"title":"","content":"I think the Red Talons benefit from nuance, as do many of the more difficult character types. Also, I think they're more identifiable than it seems. The Red Talons are angry. Not just angry; they <i>are </i>Anger. Think of all those times you've wanted to lash out angrily. Maybe just take away every gun or bomb in the world. Or wipe away politicians, start the system over. Maybe you hate the way the system favors the 1%, or can't stand that we've cut down half the world's forests since the Industrial Revolution, and deforestation is still a problem. Animal abuse. Pollution (a literal, real, terrible thing, not some vague Captain Planet concept). Crime. Disease. Ignorance leading to extinction (of wolves, say, as in their continued plight in Idaho).<br /> <br /> Every time you've gotten angry about human evils, and especially when you get so angry you want to lash out in reactionary format, you want to hate, that's what the Talons are like. All of the above, plus the keen ability to feel the world's pain. Theirs is the animal reaction you have when you lash out, only they are capable of thinking and yet feeling that overwhelming anger. They see how the Wyrm thrives in the human world, wears humanity as a shield, and also how the Garou Nation has done basically nothing to fix the problem. Of course, it's a problem that's hard to fix without complete extermination of the human race. That part the Talons understand, and while they might be only too happy to go that route, other Garou might be wise enough to know that just eradicating humans wouldn't heal the wounds left in their passing.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons are the part of you that wanted to see Michael Vick fed to his dogs. They're the part of you that just wanted to destroy your bullies. They're the part of you that hates the way everything has become so entangled, complicated and infuriating, especially for those on the bottom. They're the part that longs for something simpler, like a sunlit patch to lie in, the feel of the wind through your fur as you run unchallenged through a wild, untamed land. They exult in the most basic thrills life has to offer: a hot meal, a warm companion, a green world to enjoy.<br /> <br /> I think the Red Talons are one of the most challenging tribes to play, because you do have to reach deeper. You have to step outside your usual comfort zone. A Red Talon version of me would gladly disembowel this version of me just for sitting here writing about this stuff on my computer. It's an interesting roleplaying challenge stepping into that frame of mind, and all the more so if you want to make a character more nuanced than &quot;GRAR! RIP! SMASH! TEAR! HUMAN ARE BAD, ME WOLF AM KING!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T15:54:37-08:00","id":314013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=313943#post313943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing is, Heavy Arms, exactly the same applies to all the Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think it applies well to some of the Tribes (the Black Furies, for instance, suffer a similar problem but don't have the approachability issues and have more going for them beyond fighting for women).<br /> <br /> And nothing in your list of questions or list of &quot;representations&quot; actually counters a thing I said. It's also a continued attempt to ignore how the Red Talons are presented with how, perhaps, they should have been presented.<br /> <br /> If anything your Red Talon example, and to some extent Claire's post, reinforce my point.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons are Rage? How? What makes Red Talons more &quot;Rage&quot; than any other Tribe? Is their anger at humans greater than the Black Furies anger at men? A Get's anger at weakness?<br /> <br /> Is a Red Talon Lupus Ragabash more in touch with their Rage than a Child of Gaia Metis Ahroun? The mechanics certainly don't bare out anything of the sort. What makes a Red Talon more &quot;wild,&quot; &quot;primal,&quot; or whatever than any other Tribe (save obviously the Glasswalkers who are notable fore being out of touch with their primal side).<br /> <br /> This one of the big thing that I think the responses in their thread have largely lacked (and the books absolutely lack). It isn't just &quot;how do the Red Talons compare to the other Tribes,&quot; but also how they compare to the other splats; Breeds and Auspices included.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T17:10:28-08:00","id":314047,"title":"","content":"Okay. I shall approach from a differant angle.<br /> The RedTalons are Wyld. Humanity are Weaver ridden as a species, they have to rely on tools. Most of the other tribes, even their lupus born Garou, don't see a problem with Tools and Humanity. They use Fetishes and Talens freely and they employ the tools of humanity (and the weaver) as a matter of course, Cars, Fences, Cameras, Knives, Tents and so forth. A few tools was fine in the beginning for Man and Garou, but things are no longer fine. <br /> From the RedTalons perspective this makes the Garou weak. The RedTalons reject these things to keep the Garou string, not shackled to the Weaver and relying on the Wyrms very best pawns. <br /> Humanity is a crutch the Garou could do well without with the Apocalypse dawning. The RedTalons have been trying to remove that crutch since the Impergium ended, but their numbers were never large and their exclusive breeding with Wolves hurt them as humanity flourished. The other Garou no doubt counciled Adapt or Die which to the ideology of the Tribe chosen by Griffon became synonymous with &quot;Surrender or Die&quot;. That's why they are Primal Rage (just as their totem is). Every other Tribe in a Race that's supposed to be equal parts Human and Wolf and greater than both are mostly representative of cultural parts of Humanity, even their Lupus members embrace the humanity coloured aspects of the tribe. The Talons do not. <br /> <br /> They are angry because the wild places fell before the ravages of Man.<br /> They are angry because they tried to stop this and the other tribes looked away. <br /> They are angry because the other tribes are more Human than Wolf (in turn they embraced more Wolf than Man).<br /> They are angry because a weak species overcame the strong, raped the world and infected her guardians with their weakness. <br /> They are angry with the other Garou because they STILL don't listen (ironically think Picard in First Contact &quot;This far, no further&quot; speech).<br /> They are angry because they Know they're losing on all fronts. <br /> They are angry because loyalty failed. Alliances failed. Traditions failed. The Litany failed and the Garou failed. Anger is all that sustains them and it echoes through the ages and in Griffon. They are born of the Lupus that come to sentience and see the world in these ways and Anger and Rage carry them on.<br /> <br /> They are the Tribe that set out to do what the rest of the Nation will not. They will Hunt Man, they will deny the Weaver in all but the simplest and oldest of ways, they will champion not just Gaia but the Wyld as it is the ONLY hope against the Apocalypse and eternal destruction. <br /> <br /> I built that from the W20 and WTAr RedTalon blurb and the Book of the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-16T18:02:44-08:00","id":314072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314047#post314047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The RedTalons are Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Except they aren't. They are wild, not Wyld. They're not unhindered creativity and possibility. They're not about evolving and change. All of their anger is aimed things changing in ways they don't like.<br /> <br /> As I said before, the Red Talons would be far more compelling if they were the Wyld counterpart to the Glasswalker Weaver. If instead of being obsessed with the past and tearing down the present to reclaim the past, they were focused on making a new world where possibility wasn't being crushed by the Weaver and tainted by the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity are Weaver ridden as a species, they have to rely on tools. Most of the other tribes, even their lupus born Garou, don't see a problem with Tools and Humanity. </div> </div> </div>So, the Red Talons shtick remains, &quot;we hate humanity more than you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are angry because a weak species overcame the strong, raped the world and infected her guardians with their weakness. </div> </div> </div>That strikes me as a very poor position. The strongest animal is the winner. Humanity won because it was stronger, not because the &quot;weak&quot; won when they shouldn't have won. That's not how &quot;strong&quot; works in nature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are the Tribe that set out to do what the rest of the Nation will not. </div> </div> </div>Plenty of Tribes would claim the same thing. All of the Tribes would claim a list of things to be angry over. So this approach isn't convincing me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T05:21:10-08:00","id":314398,"title":"","content":"I don't think anyone ever will Heavy Arms. I mean the Book of the Wyld outright tells us the two tribes most connected to the Wyld are the BlackFuries and the RedTalons and how that is so in their different ways. The &quot;Weak&quot; thing isn't a poor position because without the Weaver's nigh direct interference in that single species Humanity would not have spread the way it did or come to the power that it has. Humanity's chief strength, the reason it was chosen as part of the Shifter's forms, was that of intellect and reasoning. No Claws, No Fangs, No Fur, A moderate package of senses. But that was okay because man could think, he could make claws and take fur, just like other creatures can use tools. But then the Weaver influenced them and gave them too much and the Wyrm got into them and now look at things.Take the average Man or Woman in the World of darkness (or lets face it most western countries in our own world) put them in the wild somewhere where a cell phone wont work. Dead. Humanity has gone from Apex Predator to a form of Cattle Herd creature. <br /> <br /> The Wyld itself is about endless possibility. To the RedTalons who never embraced the human heritages those possibilities exist in the most fundamental of ways. Time is measured in fluid things like the faces of the Moon or the turning of seasons, Numbers are something that is used only when needed then forgotten about again until needed again (Numbers pretty much dominate our way of life). Distances are measured in the span of a day or the length of a night, in the duration of a storm, the passing of a flock or the shifting of a wind, which change on a case by case basis. The cresting of every hill is the beginning of a new world, every meeting is like it's the first.<br /> <br /> Sure, you'll find bits of this in many Lupus in other Tribes, but they also carry the 'taint' of those tribes by connection. The RedTalons are it unfettered and guided by Griffon and yes some of their schtick will be that hatred of Humanity that gets put in our faces, and it'll always be &quot;More than You&quot; because the other Tribes don't Hate Humanity, they embrace it, they rationalize what it has done and will do, they make excuses for the ignorant. Sure they'll kill, some more unreservedly than others, but that's usually in line with dealing with some other Wyrmthing. Heck, in the World of Darkness the RedTalons for all their hatred may hold the secret to saving humanity from the Weaver and the Wyrm. Thin the Herd, rip away their Weaver Things, Expose them to the Horrors of the Corrupt and Mad Wyrm, Make them Fight Back to Survive... <br /> <br /> That's actually rather scary (since I came up with it while typing instead of any previously held view).<br /> <br /> I may not Convince you of these things heavy Arms, that they are needed as a tribe and provide a vital part of the Garou Nation (Just like the SilverFangs do and the Get of Fenris and the Children of Gaia etc) but I think this thread alone for pothers (and indeed myself) has prompted and opened up new worlds of possibility for the Tribe that Hates Humanity (ooh new horizons and possibilities... that's kinda Wyld too!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T09:16:38-08:00","id":314618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314013#post314013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Red Talons are Rage? How? What makes Red Talons more &quot;Rage&quot; than any other Tribe? Is their anger at humans greater than the Black Furies anger at men? A Get's anger at weakness?</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though this is a bad way of wording the question. What makes a Fenrir more Warrior than a Fianna? They certainly failed to beat the Fianna in open warfare. Does a Fenrir Ahroun have any mechanical advantage over a Fianna one? or a Silver Fang one? For all real purposes the only thing that makes a Get more of a &quot;Warrior&quot; than the other tribes is their society. Which is the same for the Red Talons, who specifically believe that they are Gaia's rage given form above all other tribes.<br /> <br /> It does frustrate me that, mostly due to the focus of the introductory tribe text, the Red Talons are always seen as the most one dimensional. I wonder if it isn't just because no one really cares to delve into the tribe, since every other tribe appears similarly one dimensional and potentially dull until you dig into its lore. We really aren't going to be able to objectively answer a subjective question though. There is no magic bit of evidence that will suddenly make the Red Talons seem valid if someone just doesn't like them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T13:02:37-08:00","id":314779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314398#post314398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think anyone ever will Heavy Arms.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think some of this is a bit of talking past each other. Most of my position is my problem with the Red Talons as written, not what they could be. If I were redoing the game I wouldn't remove the Red Talons, I would change them to embrace many of the potential things you see in them. The problem is that you're trying to convince me that they're OK as is with what they, essentially, could have been; but aren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I mean the Book of the Wyld outright tells us the two tribes most connected to the Wyld are the BlackFuries and the RedTalons and how that is so in their different ways. </div> </div> </div>WtA is a big game with 4ish editions worth of material, plenty of which disagrees with itself.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons are the really in touch with the Wyld? Ok... but they never are presented as actually doing anything about it. Their connection might as well be meaningless since only seems to manifest is having a few &quot;make nature take over human spaces&quot; Gifts at high Rank.<br /> <br /> For all their connection to the Wyld, they spend all their time acting like they're trying to be the Balance Wyrm in its absence (and following its path into corruption).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;Weak&quot; thing isn't a poor position because without the Weaver's nigh direct interference in that single species Humanity would not have spread the way it did or come to the power that it has. </div> </div> </div>Meh. &quot;Humans have no agency, supernaturals did it all,&quot; is something the books generally reject rather thoroughly.<br /> <br /> Humans are a strong species. Strength in nature isn't muscles, or claws, or teeth. It's survival. Survival as a species makes you strong. The aid of the Weaver only sped up what would have happened anyway. Human smarts made them strong. It let them adapt faster than species relying on natural selection only. Even without the Weaver's &quot;night direct interference&quot; humans would have displaced countless species, chasing away competing predators like wolves. Fire and stone tools is more than enough technology to humans to shape nature to their own desires.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humanity has gone from Apex Predator to a form of Cattle Herd creature. </div> </div> </div>That is, very much, not how it works.<br /> <br /> Plenty of social species have specialists. It's a natural result of large population social species. We don't need every human to be a badass to be apex predators. Because we can have physically weak humans make tools that make a small number of badass humans even more badass making us even better at killing other things (even if mostly each other these days).<br /> <br /> Ants are not weak because worker drones are defenseless without soldier drones, and the queen and young would all die without both. That interconnected system makes them incredibly strong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> To the RedTalons who never embraced the human heritages those possibilities exist in the most fundamental of ways. Time is measured in fluid things like the faces of the Moon or the turning of seasons, Numbers are something that is used only when needed then forgotten about again until needed again (Numbers pretty much dominate our way of life). Distances are measured in the span of a day or the length of a night, in the duration of a storm, the passing of a flock or the shifting of a wind, which change on a case by case basis. The cresting of every hill is the beginning of a new world, every meeting is like it's the first. </div> </div> </div>I find it funny that you're trying to make the case that the Red Talons embrace endless possibility by rejecting the possibilities within humanity. If the Red Talons were really as into possibility as they should be as Wyld focused, Whelp's Compromise would be the dominant and traditional camp of the Tribe; not a scorned bunch of liberal radicals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...and it'll always be &quot;More than You&quot; because the other Tribes don't Hate Humanity... </div> </div> </div>As has been cited earlier, the books really don't present this. The other Tribes don't hate <i>humans</i> but all agree that humanity as a whole is damaged and bad. That it's current state is unacceptable. Even the Glasswalkers generally agree with that.<br /> <br /> The difference is that the Red Talons default answer is, &quot;kill humans whenever they're a problem,&quot; and the other Tribes see a more nuanced situation.<br /> <br /> And frankly you're cherry picking a lot in these things. The Book of the Wyld says something that supports you, so nothing else seems to matter. Your summation of the Red Talon experience is pretty much exactly how lots of books describe being a lupus in general, but that doesn't matter because the Red Talons lack of human blood in them... somehow makes their version different.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314618#post314618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel as though this is a bad way of wording the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you're being terribly fair to my question.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What makes a Fenrir more Warrior than a Fianna? </div> </div> </div>Very little. The Fenrir fancy themselves as the most warrior focused Tribe, but the Garou are a warrior nation. The Get have a few minor advantages, but mostly get away with this claim more because other Tribes focus on other things, rather than other Tribes lacking the ability to match them in combat. The Red Talons don't focus on being Rage incarnate more than the other Tribes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They certainly failed to beat the Fianna in open warfare. </div> </div> </div>That's easy actually. Warfare is really hard to win when everyone on your side is a warrior. Having the strongest warrior on the battlefield means nothing if your opponent has a strategy to get around that, and the logistics and supply chains to support it, and the spies to make sure you have the right information.<br /> <br /> The Fianna might generally lose to the Fenrir in a battle of champions (though close calls), but their affinity of stories, trickery, and knowledge gives them advantages in open war besides brute strength.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does a Fenrir Ahroun have any mechanical advantage over a Fianna one? </div> </div> </div>They can. I think more telling is that non-Ahrouns are generally going to favor the Get for having better combat mechanics available to them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T13:41:20-08:00","id":314798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314779#post314779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Red Talons don't focus on being Rage incarnate more than the other Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll just have to respectfully disagree, considering the Red Talon gift tree is basically kill efficiently, inspire fear, inspiring delerium, and regain rage, and pile on combat bonuses while in frenzy.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T13:57:37-08:00","id":314801,"title":"","content":"For the assumptions of Werewolf, not every form of &quot;adaptation&quot; is necessarily a pure manifestation or tie to the Wyld. In fact, it would be better to describe humans as industrious and hard-working than adaptable as such. They codebreak behavior and see connections readily, but this isn't the sort of possibility that the Wyld necessarily finds kinship or favor with, on account of how many assumptions behind the technology which humans develop stay the same, particularly at the most basic levels. Keep in mind that manifestations of the Wyld include Rorg's Hungry Children, aka meteorites that eat people, blurring the lines between what's assumed to be living and not living. This is one of the less notable things that the Wyld does. Bigger feats include stripping away even foundations of spiritual identity, which causes immense destruction when it occurs.<br /> <br /> And in this, Red Talons embrace the Wyld, because the sort of change it embodies is better than their current dismal state. They quite literally have nothing to lose from having the rug yanked out from under the world they know. The rug already got pulled out, and they're still trying to struggle back up to stand. A sudden change that changes the meaning of what solid ground and standing up mean would benefit them and harm the edifice built by humans, and which, having embraced the world before humans came and lamented the loss of the land and fallen species, they have grown to hate so.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I don't think that it's really a situation of Glass Walker to Weaver and Red Talon to Wyld, but of to homid and lupus. The Triatic connection is tenuous, but the connection of heritage is strong. The fact that the Glass Walkers still have lupus but the Red Talons don't have homids stands as testament to an inherent imbalance with the human condition in Werewolf, possibly related to statements about cultural assimilation and resistance to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:20:21-08:00","id":314956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314798#post314798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll just have to respectfully disagree, considering the Red Talon gift tree is basically kill efficiently, inspire fear, inspiring delerium, and regain rage, and pile on combat bonuses while in frenzy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The only solid example in there are the Frenzy bonuses. Though Metis in general have them beat on the &quot;embodying Rage&quot; mechanics. And all the Tribes have &quot;kill shit better&quot; Gifts. Even the Children of Gaia have offense combat Gifts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314801#post314801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the assumptions of Werewolf, not every form of &quot;adaptation&quot; is necessarily a pure manifestation or tie to the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure how you really make that case when we're talking about biological adaptations. Not pure? Absolutely, but an adaptation is a change given form. It is, metaphysically, how Wyld to Weaver is supposed to happen on that scale.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In fact, it would be better to describe humans as industrious and hard-working than adaptable as such. </div> </div> </div>Humans are both industrious and adaptable. Just being one doesn't get you to us.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Keep in mind that manifestations of the Wyld include Rorg's Hungry Children, aka meteorites that eat people, blurring the lines between what's assumed to be living and not living. This is one of the less notable things that the Wyld does. Bigger feats include stripping away even foundations of spiritual identity, which causes immense destruction when it occurs. </div> </div> </div>So... how does this not counter your point?<br /> <br /> What other species has started to blur the line between living and not living? We're building technology that mimics life and approaching the point where the lines are growing remarkably thin and arbitrary. We add non-living things into our living bodies as functional components. What are the Red Talons doing that blurs these lines?<br /> <br /> What other species even has the concept of a spiritual identity? That has invented philosophies that have lead to both personal and large scale destruction?<br /> <br /> These aren't concepts we see without humans. Even in the WOD. Even in the WtA specific aspects of it because the Garou and Fera are bringing humanness into the equation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And in this, Red Talons embrace the Wyld, because the sort of change it embodies is better than their current dismal state. </div> </div> </div>How do the embrace it? This is a compelling case for <i>why they should</i>. But nothing they're written as doing actually makes them as moving forward in this direction.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Additionally, I don't think that it's really a situation of Glass Walker to Weaver and Red Talon to Wyld, but of to homid and lupus. </div> </div> </div>My point on this is that making the Red Talons more compelling would be accomplished by focusing on that dynamic over the current status of the Red Talons in the books.<br /> <br /> I don't think any higher level commentary the no-homid Red Talons as-is really helps make them interesting to play. This is, after all, what inspired the thread. Not, &quot;What conceptual ideas to Red Talons bring to the game,&quot; but, &quot;why don't people play them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Answering, &quot;why should I play a Red Talon?&quot; with, &quot;They bring an important statement on the imbalance of human and wolf in the setting,&quot; is not a compelling case to why they're fun to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T17:43:43-08:00","id":314963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314956#post314956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how you really make that case when we're talking about biological adaptations. Not pure? Absolutely, but an adaptation is a change given form. It is, metaphysically, how Wyld to Weaver is supposed to happen on that scale.</div> </div> </div> </div>We stopped talking about biological traits alone when you started talking about knapping flint.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Humans are both industrious and adaptable. Just being one doesn't get you to us. </div> </div> </div>Not by this definition scheme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So... how does this not counter your point?<br /> <br /> What other species has started to blur the line between living and not living? We're building technology that mimics life and approaching the point where the lines are growing remarkably thin and arbitrary. We add non-living things into our living bodies as functional components. What are the Red Talons doing that blurs these lines? </div> </div> </div>I'm discounting your assessment that technology is Wyld-ish just because it progresses. Incidentally, we aren't anywhere near blurring the lines of an inanimate chunk of stone and a living being. It's all a bit difficult to process through this fictional setting, but what the Wyld represents in this instance is a complete lack of care for whether or not rocks aren't alive in the first place. A fundamental change in an assumption, rather than working through any form of technology based on established laws of physics, biochemical principles, or other concerns. It's more than just something that wasn't yet discovered, being the relatively light touch of a spiritual force that does things that might not work out the same all of the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What other species even has the concept of a spiritual identity? That has invented philosophies that have lead to both personal and large scale destruction? </div> </div> </div>Doesn't ,matter. The core concept of Werewolf is &quot;Humans should sit down, shut up and listen to the world.&quot; This also nicely encompasses my growing irritation with the topic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> These aren't concepts we see without humans. Even in the WOD. Even in the WtA specific aspects of it because the Garou and Fera are bringing humanness into the equation. </div> </div> </div>The Nameless accomplishes things that humans can't even contemplate as part of being at the upper-end of statted Wyldlings. It also suggests that the spiritual essence which it deals with is not something of a philosophy, but an understanding that comes up from within, if you will. Another arena where humans overthinking things blinds them in this setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do the embrace it? This is a compelling case for <i>why they should</i>. But nothing they're written as doing actually makes them as moving forward in this direction. </div> </div> </div>By not building elaborate societies that are vulnerable to being torn down like most human cultures are? And particularly those that rely on infrastructure? You can't embrace the Wyld by building up infrastructure. You can embrace the Wyld by upending the overbuilt infrastructure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My point on this is that making the Red Talons more compelling would be accomplished by focusing on that dynamic over the current status of the Red Talons in the books.<br /> <br /> I don't think any higher level commentary the no-homid Red Talons as-is really helps make them interesting to play. This is, after all, what inspired the thread. Not, &quot;What conceptual ideas to Red Talons bring to the game,&quot; but, &quot;why don't people play them.&quot;<br /> <br /> Answering, &quot;why should I play a Red Talon?&quot; with, &quot;They bring an important statement on the imbalance of human and wolf in the setting,&quot; is not a compelling case to why they're fun to play. </div> </div> </div>My answer would be, &quot;Because there's lots of weird shit in the deep wilderness that humans never see. Even homid and metis Garou tend to get agitated and go home before they find it, being tied to different septs, their human kin, and spirits that still have some expectation of ceremonial reverence that is best served through human social practices.&quot; When you go full wolf, you run around everywhere, and happen upon the places where humans wouldn't even think to go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T19:33:09-08:00","id":315018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=314963#post314963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We stopped talking about biological traits alone when you started talking about knapping flint.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tool use and learned skills are biological capabilities. Humans are not the only animals with these capabilities. Wolves, for example, have to teach their young skills and behaviors. They don't actually do everything by instinct (a lot of early behavioral studies of wolves were horridly off because they were based on captured wolves that were thrown together in zoos without the continuity of family and training that wild packs have).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not by this definition scheme. </div> </div> </div>Perhaps you should set a specific scheme. At the moment it just seems like you're shifting definitions as it suits your arguments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm discounting your assessment that technology is Wyld-ish just because it progresses. </div> </div> </div>That's not my argument or assessment.<br /> <br /> My point is that humans are not actually out of touch with the Wyld and some still bring that creative possibility into technology creating new things, rather than being stuck in the stasis of the Weaver. And that humans, as a whole, do far more that is in line with the Wyld than the Red Talons are actually portrayed as doing. The Red Talons don't do what you're saying is Wyld-like, and what you're saying is Wyld like is something at least some humans do.<br /> <br /> In other words, the Red Talons, as written, suck at doing anything with their connection to the Wyld because humans do way more with what little connection they have to it than the Red Talons do with their stated massive connection. Which is why I've advocated for making the Red Talons more Wyld in their actions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's all a bit difficult to process through this fictional setting, but what the Wyld represents in this instance is a complete lack of care for whether or not rocks aren't alive in the first place. </div> </div> </div>The Wyld has no concept of time. It works as fast or as slow as suits its unfathomable whims. Some Wyld changes are instant, some take time and steps. Trying to classify everything Wyld as a radical and fundamental change is limiting the Wyld in ways not supported in the books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The core concept of Werewolf is &quot;Humans should sit down, shut up and listen to the world.&quot; </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's not the core concept of the game in the slightest... because that's not what the books say is the core concept of the game, which is mostly focused on playing creatures caught between to worlds which allows us to explore the consequences of human activity on personal to cosmic levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This also nicely encompasses my growing irritation with the topic. </div> </div> </div>You can stop posting anytime. If you want to backhandedly tell me to shut up, you're just communicating to me that you're frustrated because you've been challenged and can't actually respond with something meaningful.<br /> <br /> If you actually had some citation from the books to slap down and leave me with no response but to concede a point... you'd have done so already.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> By not building elaborate societies that are vulnerable to being torn down like most human cultures are? And particularly those that rely on infrastructure? You can't embrace the Wyld by building up infrastructure. You can embrace the Wyld by upending the overbuilt infrastructure. </div> </div> </div>So the Red Talons do nothing. They don't do what humans do, doesn't equate to them doing Wyld things. And undoing Weaver things is what the Balance Wyrm is for, not the Wyld. The Wyld creates new things, not destroys the old. You aren't embracing the Wyld by upending overbuilt infrastructure. You're embracing the Balance Wyrm. The Wyld would just create new things and spam reality with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My answer would be, &quot;Because there's lots of weird shit in the deep wilderness that humans never see. Even homid and metis Garou tend to get agitated and go home before they find it, being tied to different septs, their human kin, and spirits that still have some expectation of ceremonial reverence that is best served through human social practices.&quot; When you go full wolf, you run around everywhere, and happen upon the places where humans wouldn't even think to go. </div> </div> </div>Sounds like why I should play a Silent Strider Lupus.<br /> <br /> Red Talons are still territorial and stick to their Sept and their wolf-kin. They still have spiritual duties to the local spirits of their territory. They aren't explorers of the deep areas, they're out in the deep wilderness by force.<br /> <br /> The Striders are the ones that go exploring and wandering unfettered by being tied to one place. And plenty of Tribes have Camps that focus on exploring the wilderness and Wyld places: The Freebooters, the Daughters of Demeter, the Seekers of the Lost Tribes, the Children of Dire, the Whispering Rovers, the Umbral Pilots, the Seekers (more than most Strides), the Ana-gamin, the Trance Runners, the World Tree, the Scouts, the Skywalkers, and the Wyld Children. So yeah.. the Red Talons are not actually offering anything unique in &quot;weird shit in the deep Wilderness that humans never see,&quot; since lots of Tribes besides the Red Talons have members out exploring those places.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T21:03:42-08:00","id":315050,"title":"","content":"I just started a new game with my colleagues here on campus. In preparation for the game, I lent them my books for a couple days. They were excited to play, because it seemed like it could be cathartic.<br /> <br /> Using <i><b>only</b></i> the W20 book, is it unfair for all five brand-new players to get the same impression of the Talons? To disclose all information about the group, none are native English speakers, yet they all expressed a dislike for the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T21:17:02-08:00","id":315052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315018#post315018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tool use and learned skills are biological capabilities. Humans are not the only animals with these capabilities. Wolves, for example, have to teach their young skills and behaviors. They don't actually do everything by instinct (a lot of early behavioral studies of wolves were horridly off because they were based on captured wolves that were thrown together in zoos without the continuity of family and training that wild packs have).</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. But the infrastructure that follows, that's more a function of how much indoctrination you can fit in a human skull, which is only vaguely biological. Does it involve the brain? Sure. But it's not a really direct sort of relation. Humans believe what they're told. What they are told depends on a huge cultural infodump, which has a sort of existence outside of biology even though it occupies space inside brains.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Perhaps you should set a specific scheme. At the moment it just seems like you're shifting definitions as it suits your arguments. </div> </div> </div>There are no real arguments here. This really does just boil down to taste, at this point. More on that later.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not my argument or assessment.<br /> <br /> My point is that humans are not actually out of touch with the Wyld and some still bring that creative possibility into technology creating new things, rather than being stuck in the stasis of the Weaver. And that humans, as a whole, do far more that is in line with the Wyld than the Red Talons are actually portrayed as doing. The Red Talons don't do what you're saying is Wyld-like, and what you're saying is Wyld like is something at least some humans do. </div> </div> </div>You readily forget that the setting info explicitly states that humans are out of touch with the Wyld and even the creative possibility of technology is because it's the least restrictive of the Weaver's sides, which is a different thing from the most restrictive part of the Wyld, if such a concept even makes sense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In other words, the Red Talons, as written, suck at doing anything with their connection to the Wyld because humans do way more with what little connection they have to it than the Red Talons do with their stated massive connection. Which is why I've advocated for making the Red Talons more Wyld in their actions. </div> </div> </div>If you can even pin down what that means. The same force that gave rise to Rorg's Hungry Children does stuff just 'cause. The tumult would be welcomed by a culture that wasn't, existing yet unfettered by a history of settlements and such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Wyld has no concept of time. It works as fast or as slow as suits its unfathomable whims. Some Wyld changes are instant, some take time and steps. Trying to classify everything Wyld as a radical and fundamental change is limiting the Wyld in ways not supported in the books. </div> </div> </div>That doesn't even follow from what I was getting at there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm pretty sure that's not the core concept of the game in the slightest... because that's not what the books say is the core concept of the game, which is mostly focused on playing creatures caught between to worlds which allows us to explore the consequences of human activity on personal to cosmic levels. </div> </div> </div>Not one book goes by where the setting quite unironically admonishes humans for sucking and for shitting up the world. They're so spiritually ignorant that they would need to sit at the feet of the Apis to actually live with the spirits and not fuck shit up. This is not really an esoteric detail of the setting, either. It's behind every bunch of clueless humans that meddled with spirits because they thought they were communing with a higher power. It's behind the reason that Jeremiah Lassiter got possessed and turned Premium Oil into what became Pentex. It's why humans don't care that they're rotting on the inside in the setting of Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You can stop posting anytime. If you want to backhandedly tell me to shut up, you're just communicating to me that you're frustrated because you've been challenged and can't actually respond with something meaningful.<br /> <br /> If you actually had some citation from the books to slap down and leave me with no response but to concede a point... you'd have done so already. </div> </div> </div>Lots of people have swung by to try and &quot;fix&quot; things, but in a lot of cases it seems like fixing it would destroy it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So the Red Talons do nothing. They don't do what humans do, doesn't equate to them doing Wyld things. And undoing Weaver things is what the Balance Wyrm is for, not the Wyld. The Wyld creates new things, not destroys the old. You aren't embracing the Wyld by upending overbuilt infrastructure. You're embracing the Balance Wyrm. The Wyld would just create new things and spam reality with them. </div> </div> </div>Actually, the original conception probably had something to do with the cynical notion that they can't stop acting like humans even though none of them are human. Incidentally, the act of balancing in Werewolf would promote the Wyld. Don't get fooled into thinking that the answer to undoing the Weaver is actually found in the middle path. It's taken over so much territory that a shift in favor of balance would be one in favor of the Wyld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sounds like why I should play a Silent Strider Lupus. </div> </div> </div>You mean the haunted tribe of ghostly wolves with huge amounts of baggage from Ancient Egypt and a crossover entanglement with Robert E. Howard Set-worshipping vampires? I don't think so. Even the wildest of lupus from the Striders is still going to have a heavy Anpw flavor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Red Talons are still territorial and stick to their Sept and their wolf-kin. They still have spiritual duties to the local spirits of their territory. They aren't explorers of the deep areas, they're out in the deep wilderness by force. </div> </div> </div>And it's there that there are still monsters that don't make it to civilization. Have you not ever read Ways of the Wolf?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Striders are the ones that go exploring and wandering unfettered by being tied to one place. </div> </div> </div>Except that they totally don't want to do this, have massive amounts of human cultural baggage, and are constantly looking to reclaim Egypt, if possible. Also, no Ancestors for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And plenty of Tribes have Camps that focus on exploring the wilderness and Wyld places: The Freebooters, the Daughters of Demeter, the Seekers of the Lost Tribes </div> </div> </div>Tiny splinter groups, all very much entrenched in deeply human customs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , the Children of Dire </div> </div> </div>A dumb idea that shouldn't exist because Hispo isn't a dire wolf and no one knew what dire wolves were until paleontologists exhumed them from their exclusively New World habitat (European population of dire wolves across all of prehistory: 0). The only way that they could fit in the setting in the slightest is if they were excised from the Fianna and made into a cross-breed camp of Uktena and Nuwisha. And it would still be dumb, because dire wolves didn't give rise to modern wolves, hence why the Nuwisha come into play here - the closest relative the dire wolf had among its still-living cousins was the coyote.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , the Whispering Rovers, </div> </div> </div>Very entrenched in human culture.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Umbral Pilots, </div> </div> </div>Get that steampunk out of here!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Seekers (more than most Strides), the Ana-gamin, the Trance Runners, the World Tree, the Scouts, the Skywalkers, and the Wyld Children. So yeah.. the Red Talons are not actually offering anything unique in &quot;weird shit in the deep Wilderness that humans never see,&quot; since lots of Tribes besides the Red Talons have members out exploring those places. </div> </div> </div>If you want to go against the Revised Tribebook, sure. All those groups are still tied to human groups. None of them actually offers the prospect of never having been human or even being descended from a human culture, even if a human-like one arose among them. You aren't so strange that those cultures won't welcome you as lost family.<br /> <br /> You don't want a tribe full of wolfweres, whatever. I'm not convinced that this isn't your personal taste, since you continuously attempt to pull more for humans regarding the Wyld than what the setting has made absolutely crystal clear - they're completely in the wrong. They help structure things, which the Weaver likes. The Defiler, in turn, loves this, because it can much more easily slip down and dirty the world through the strands of the Weaver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-18-2014, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T00:12:06-08:00","id":315102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315050#post315050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using <i><b>only</b></i> the W20 book, is it unfair for all five brand-new players to get the same impression of the Talons? To disclose all information about the group, none are native English speakers, yet they all expressed a dislike for the tribe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lemme guess... your players are all human, right?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T00:40:25-08:00","id":315131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315102#post315102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lemme guess... your players are all human, right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course. No pets are allowed according to the lease for my flat.<br /> But lemme guess, the harmless question I asked won't be answered, or my players' personal character will be the target? C'mon, I was asking an honest question:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Using <i><b>only</b></i> the W20 book, is it unfair for all five brand-new players to get the same impression of the Talons? To disclose all information about the group, none are native English speakers, yet they all expressed a dislike for the tribe. </div> </div> </div>Simple yes or no, that's all. I did state, as shown above, that English is not their native language (Slovenian, Spanish, Arabic, Chinese), and thus could be an error in interpretation. Yet despite vastly different language groups, they came up with the same opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T01:04:07-08:00","id":315139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315052#post315052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You readily forget that the setting info explicitly states that humans are out of touch with the Wyld and even the creative possibility of technology is because it's the least restrictive of the Weaver's sides, which is a different thing from the most restrictive part of the Wyld, if such a concept even makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books explicitly state the the humans have an incredibly weak connection to the Wyld compared to the dominance the Weaver and the Wyrm have on them. Not that they're completely gone from it. It means that the sparks of the Wyld still in humans get quickly gobbled up by the Weaver, yes, but it doesn't mean that the Wyld isn't there. Remember, life, and all of existence in the WtA cosmology, is supposed to be a balance of the Triat with everything being touched by all three. The whole universe is out of whack with the Weaver and Wyrm no longer fulfilling their proper roles. Humans are just excellent metaphysical conduits for this larger cosmological problem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you can even pin down what that means. </div> </div> </div>The Red Talons creating and changing to bring about a world that regains balance by bringing more Wyld into it until it is as strong as the Weaver and Wyrm again, instead of the Red Talons just trying to defending stagnant wildernesses and tear down the Weaver and Wyrm to regain balance.<br /> <br /> It's not hard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That doesn't even follow from what I was getting at there. </div> </div> </div>My point is that you're on one hand making claims about how the Wyld does things, even while you acknowledge that the Wyld can't actually be summed up like that. Yes, the Wyld makes predatory rocks floating around in space. And flips gravity on you instantly. It also does small things like give you six fingers, or cause a minor mutation that doesn't have an effect for six generations of a species.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not one book goes by where the setting quite unironically admonishes humans for sucking and for shitting up the world. </div> </div> </div>The books also put plenty of blame on other things, as well as making it clear that humans are redeemable as a species.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's why humans don't care that they're rotting on the inside in the setting of Werewolf. </div> </div> </div>Except for all the ones that do...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Lots of people have swung by to try and &quot;fix&quot; things, but in a lot of cases it seems like fixing it would destroy it. </div> </div> </div>Oh? What's actually wrong with my suggestions on fixing the Red Talons to make them more about embracing the Wyld. About creating change and new things. Mining the past of crazy diversity their Totem represents for new species and new creatures to bring into the world, until natural processes finds ones that can adapt to the world humans have brought about and be stronger than humanity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You mean the haunted tribe of ghostly wolves with huge amounts of baggage from Ancient Egypt and a crossover entanglement with Robert E. Howard Set-worshipping vampires? I don't think so. Even the wildest of lupus from the Striders is still going to have a heavy Anpw flavor. </div> </div> </div>None of which stops them from delving deep into the wilds and Wyld places, and encountering weird and strange things. Playing a Strider is saying, &quot;yeah I want to play weird strange encounters as I wander the spaces between both cities and Septs.&quot; The Red Talons don't have that built in.<br /> <br /> You're shifting your goal posts. You said that the appeal of the Red Talons is exploring the strangeness of the deep wilderness and the Wyld places. You made a canonically false statement that homids and metis don't go there for reasons that aren't actually unique to any breed (and ignoring that there are metis Red Talons that this is supposed to be a sale for as well).<br /> <br /> There is nothing in the books saying that a lupus Silent Strider can't go to places a lupus Red Talon can go. There's a lot of things that say that the Strider is likely to have been to more places and seen more weird shit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it's there that there are still monsters that don't make it to civilization. Have you not ever read Ways of the Wolf? </div> </div> </div>See, here's the thing about Ways of the Wolf. It's not, &quot;Ways of the Red Talons.&quot; It's about all lupus. It applies to homids that want to reject their human sides and live as wolves instead (hey there's even a Camp for that!).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except that they totally don't want to do this, have massive amounts of human cultural baggage, and are constantly looking to reclaim Egypt, if possible. Also, no Ancestors for you. </div> </div> </div>The Red Talons don't want to do it either. The human cultural baggage only matters as much as you want it to (my last Strider was a lupus, and the only human cultural baggage he had was a Deed name that fit the Tribe's standards and having to deal with humans when around them). The Striders are explicitly not all worried about reclaiming Egypt, that's a specific camp's deal. And Ancestors aren't part of your sale on what makes Red Talons interesting. Frankly, Ancestors is actually fairly weak for Red Talons (the Background isn't that strong in the first place, and Red Talons reject a large number of Abilities leaving them lots of dots in their main deals anyway making the risk of botching not worth a few bonus dice).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tiny splinter groups, all very much entrenched in deeply human customs.<br /> ...<br /> Very entrenched in human culture. </div> </div> </div>Meaningless. Human culture doesn't stop you from going into the deep wilderness areas, Wyld areas, and odd parts of the Umbra and dealing with the crazy shit the books have hiding out there. Your sale of playing the Red Talons is undermined by the large presence of &quot;human&quot; Tribes with Camps that do this despite your claim that they don't offer this possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A dumb idea that shouldn't exist because Hispo isn't a dire wolf and no one knew what dire wolves were until paleontologists exhumed them from their exclusively New World habitat (European population of dire wolves across all of prehistory: 0). The only way that they could fit in the setting in the slightest is if they were excised from the Fianna and made into a cross-breed camp of Uktena and Nuwisha. And it would still be dumb, because dire wolves didn't give rise to modern wolves, hence why the Nuwisha come into play here - the closest relative the dire wolf had among its still-living cousins was the coyote. </div> </div> </div>What... does this have to do with the Camp?<br /> <br /> The Camp are mainly lupus Fianna that act as roving protectors of the wilderness and wolf packs. They're basically the Fianna version of the Warders of the Land, save that they'll let homids that are willing to prove themselves join up, and they don't stick to single Septs/Caerns so they can do their duties over a greater range. They are exactly the kind of PCs that fit into your sale for the Red Talons... without being Red Talons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Get that steampunk out of here! </div> </div> </div>No. If that's the best you got... you might as well admit you don't have anything and stop. The point is that even the Glasswalkers the least Wyld Tribe there is, still manages to have members going out into the deep dark places of the world. Being homids doesn't actually stop them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to go against the Revised Tribebook, sure. All those groups are still tied to human groups. None of them actually offers the prospect of never having been human or even being descended from a human culture, even if a human-like one arose among them. You aren't so strange that those cultures won't welcome you as lost family. </div> </div> </div>Shifting goal posts...<br /> <br /> And you're going against all the other Tribebooks by saying only the Red Talons go into the deep wilderness and Wyld places. Because they clearly aren't unique in that They're aren't even the only Lupus that focus on that over &quot;human&quot; cultural concerns.<br /> <br /> Maybe... you need to reread Way of the Wolf and the other lupus focused material on how lupus interact with their homid Tribemates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You don't want a tribe full of wolfweres, whatever. </div> </div> </div>I said that when?<br /> <br /> My problem with the Red Talons has never been that they lack homids. My problem is that they fail to offer anything that you can't do with the other Tribes combined with an exceedingly shallow philosophy and failure to embrace the qualities that could make them more unique and interesting at a Tribe.<br /> <br /> To illustrate my point. 1e Black Furies were also like this to me. They're just man hating TERFs. Revised managed to actually expand them and embrace more than that aspect of the Tribe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...since you continuously attempt to pull more for humans regarding the Wyld than what the setting has made absolutely crystal clear - they're completely in the wrong. They help structure things, which the Weaver likes. The Defiler, in turn, loves this, because it can much more easily slip down and dirty the world through the strands of the Weaver. </div> </div> </div>This makes me think you're too busy trying to &quot;prove&quot; me wrong than paying attention to what I said.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T01:42:40-08:00","id":315194,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315131#post315131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple yes or no, that's all. I did state, as shown above, that English is not their native language (Slovenian, Spanish, Arabic, Chinese), and thus could be an error in interpretation. Yet despite vastly different language groups, they came up with the same opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it is not unfair.<br /> <br /> That's sort of the point that sparked this thread. A lot of people don't like playing the Red Talons. They're presented in a fairly off-putting way, with a focus on what's probably their least compelling theme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T08:36:50-08:00","id":315425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315131#post315131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course. No pets are allowed according to the lease for my flat.<br /> But lemme guess, the harmless question I asked won't be answered, or my players' personal character will be the target? C'mon, I was asking an honest question:</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoah, there. Monosyllabic responses don't make for interesting discussion, do they? What I was getting at is humans, not wolves, play Werewolf: the Apocalypse. As such, your players aren't empathizing with the Red Talon mindset because you are all very comfortably human. You aren't seeing the wild places shrink before your eyes or feeling Gaia screaming in agony beneath your paws. You aren't watching your relatives get shot or poisoned. You can't walk into the umbra and feel the choking influence of the Weaver throttle the very soul of the world.<br /> <br /> The Impergium was preferable to the impending Apocalypse, brought on by the naked apes.<br /> <br /> Edit: Ironically, the Talon's bloody-minded response (Kill the Wyrm-hearted monkeys!) is also severely lacking in understanding and empathy. You might not like playing them, and that is understandable, but the Talons are an important study in what it means to be the Other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3695,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","user":"The Laughing Stranger","date":". 11-18-2014, 11:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T08:58:44-08:00","id":315448,"title":"","content":"Still doesn't answer my question, really. I asked if it was unfair for them to draw that conclusion with the <i><b>text that was written in W20</b></i>, including the Camps in the back.<br /> <br /> Couple of interesting facts (at least, to me):<br /> <br /> 1. My players are agro-ecologists and forestry researchers here in Helsinki.<br /> 2. Four of the five picked Lupus. I had to wildly change my game, dragging it from the Middle East to Austria (my players' choice of setting, as they're all comfortably European), but for the most part, it's been fun. I'll save all of The Cat Came Back's suggestions for a future game. They were awesome.<br /> <br /> Going by the W20 book alone, the Red Talons are shown to be monsters to my players. We don't have access to any of the old material. Just W20 and Changing Breeds (none of which appeal to them, either). So we don't have access to all the past lore and knowledge of the tribe and what they <i>could</i> be. I just joined a game where one of the pack mates is a Red Talon. I want to see how it goes. I'm sure I'll learn otherwise.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T08:58:55-08:00","id":315449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315050#post315050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using <i><b>only</b></i> the W20 book, is it unfair for all five brand-new players to get the same impression of the Talons?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is completely fair. I don't believe the Red Talons have much going for them without the Tribebook and errata that actually makes their archetype valid. With just the W20 alone, they don't have enough to solidify an identity. Even with Tribebook: Red Talon, it's not until Rank 2 or 3 that they really start feeling different from a Black Fury or a Fenrir. That's about the time when the Fenrir start focusing on combat buffs and the Red Talon's start packing on extra temp rage and frenzy bonuses. <br /> <br /> I always got the impression that they wanted a place where the White Howler gifts would actually see use, and so Metis and Red Talon were where they decided to dump them all since you normally wouldn't get to use them outside a Dark Ages game.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T10:03:28-08:00","id":315498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315448#post315448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still doesn't answer my question, really. I asked if it was unfair for them to draw that conclusion with the <i><b>text that was written in W20</b></i>, including the Camps in the back.<br /> <br /> Couple of interesting facts (at least, to me):<br /> <br /> 1. My players are agro-ecologists and forestry researchers here in Helsinki.<br /> 2. Four of the five picked Lupus. I had to wildly change my game, dragging it from the Middle East to Austria (my players' choice of setting, as they're all comfortably European), but for the most part, it's been fun. I'll save all of The Cat Came Back's suggestions for a future game. They were awesome.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Those do help (fellow Finn, too, hi ^^). And do make things interesting.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the text solely in W20 can easily make the Talons seem monstrous. The revisited tribebook Red Talons -can- help, but its is veery into animal mind and reasoning, though I think with you players, that might not be that hard to deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:02:47-08:00","id":315527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315448#post315448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still doesn't answer my question, really. I asked if it was unfair for them to draw that conclusion with the <i><b>text that was written in W20</b></i>, including the Camps in the back.<br /> <br /> Couple of interesting facts (at least, to me):<br /> <br /> 1. My players are agro-ecologists and forestry researchers here in Helsinki.<br /> 2. Four of the five picked Lupus. I had to wildly change my game, dragging it from the Middle East to Austria (my players' choice of setting, as they're all comfortably European), but for the most part, it's been fun. I'll save all of The Cat Came Back's suggestions for a future game. They were awesome.<br /> <br /> Going by the W20 book alone, the Red Talons are shown to be monsters to my players. We don't have access to any of the old material. Just W20 and Changing Breeds (none of which appeal to them, either). So we don't have access to all the past lore and knowledge of the tribe and what they <i>could</i> be. I just joined a game where one of the pack mates is a Red Talon. I want to see how it goes. I'm sure I'll learn otherwise.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You keep stressing that W20 and Changing Breeds are the only resources you are using, and that given those sources, the Talons seem monstrous- my response is that they should seem monstrous! Garou, especially the Red Talons, are inhuman monsters. Bloody retaliation against the encroaching Wyrm-deluded humans is more than justified: the Apocalypse has come early for the all-lupus Talons. They are fighting for their homes, their relatives and their lives. You bet they are going to respond with savagery.<br /> <br /> That said, your group sounds awesome! Sorry to jump to conclusions regarding you or your players. You might want to pick up Ways of the Wolf, with all those Lupus characters. It isn't expensive from the after-market retailers I found... and it is a pretty darn good book, to boot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:12:04-08:00","id":315533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315498#post315498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those do help (fellow Finn, too, hi ^^). And do make things interesting.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the text solely in W20 can easily make the Talons seem monstrous. The revisited tribebook Red Talons -can- help, but its is veery into animal mind and reasoning, though I think with you players, that might not be that hard to deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not a Finn, but happy to be residing here in Helsinki. I'll gladly pretend to be one that has trouble speaking the native language...?<br /> <br /> I got some good answers to my question, and I just wanted to get people thinking. I mean, if five people with vastly different languages read something in English and come up with the same interpretation, then the Talons are likely very one-dimensional as portrayed in the books. I don't think it's helpful to say &quot;Well, I played a Talon, and he was <i>nothing</i> like that!&quot; Seems like it's getting into religious apologetics.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4123-rall-bashir","name":"Rall Bashir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T11:52:05-08:00","id":315576,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that the one-dimensionality focuses to much on the kill humans part, and not enough on the inhuman monstrosity part. The Red Talon gift list is pretty scary... lots of ways to make people disapear, or die of mysterious causes. These come alongside gifts based around losing yourself to frenzy. There are gifts aimed toward Red Talon Theurges where nature itself springs up out of shere rage and visciously attacks Gaia's enemies. All said and done, there is a reason why you don't see many of them in city campaigns - it's hard to frenzy in a city without breaking the Litany.<br /> <br /> Since this thread was originally about &quot;what could make the Red Talons more popular?&quot;<br /> <br /> One aspect of the Red Talons that is sorely needed, which is relegated to side books, is that they're one of the only tribes on good terms with the Mokole. Red Talons' can actually buy a gift that summons help from a local clutch of Were-crocodiles. As a result, the Red Talons tend to hold on to really ancient knowledge that other Garou don't have access to through their ancestors... stuff only a Mokole would remember. If the W20 book focused some on their connection to the ancient times with forgotten rites, and less on the Impergium, they'd probly come off as less flat.<br /> <br /> Edited Afterthought:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315018#post315018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only solid example in there are the Frenzy bonuses. Though Metis in general have them beat on the &quot;embodying Rage&quot; mechanics. And all the Tribes have &quot;kill shit better&quot; Gifts. Even the Children of Gaia have offense combat Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't agree here either. As far as the breed options go Metis get a weird focus on being metamorphs that take the aspects of other animals, not being taken by rage and frenzy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4297,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","user":"ExplodingJoe","date":". 11-18-2014, 03:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T13:18:47-08:00","id":315672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315576#post315576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One aspect of the Red Talons that is sorely needed, which is relegated to side books, is that they're one of the only tribes on good terms with the Mokole. Red Talons' can actually buy a gift that summons help from a local clutch of Were-crocodiles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Crocodile Pact is a Kucha Ekundu Gift, not a general Red Talon Gift.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As far as the breed options go Metis get a weird focus on being metamorphs that take the aspects of other animals, not being taken by rage and frenzy. </div> </div> </div>Primal Anger, Curse of Hatred, Shell (though more a sign of their control over their Rage since they can both give themselves more and shut it off), and Lash of Rage are all Metis Gifts (and just the W20 core ones) that are about the Metis focus on Rage. We can throw Madness in even though it isn't a specifically Rage theme Gift, but for a fair comparison the Red Talon Gifts: Wolf at the Door, Beastmind, Shadows of the Impergium and Howl of Death.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-18T15:21:45-08:00","id":315719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rall Bashir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315533#post315533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got some good answers to my question, and I just wanted to get people thinking. I mean, if five people with vastly different languages read something in English and come up with the same interpretation, then the Talons are likely very one-dimensional as portrayed in the books. I don't think it's helpful to say &quot;Well, I played a Talon, and he was <i>nothing</i> like that!&quot; Seems like it's getting into religious apologetics.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I wouldn't say its apologetic. I think its more the players focusing on a different aspect of the tribe than the human killing. Like, pack unity, its really hard to form packs in online games, but Talons often can bite down their dislike and pack because its what wolves -do-. That, and the tribe IS one of the best defenders of untouched wilds, that means they can get around much easier in the nature.<br /> <br /> That, and even though more traditonal Talons dislike it, Red Talons have Cape Dog AND Dingo members. So they are willing to be in places where no wolves are found, to protect Gaia.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315576#post315576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since this thread was originally about &quot;what could make the Red Talons more popular?&quot;<br /> <br /> One aspect of the Red Talons that is sorely needed, which is relegated to side books, is that they're one of the only tribes on good terms with the Mokole. Red Talons' can actually buy a gift that summons help from a local clutch of Were-crocodiles. As a result, the Red Talons tend to hold on to really ancient knowledge that other Garou don't have access to through their ancestors... stuff only a Mokole would remember. If the W20 book focused some on their connection to the ancient times with forgotten rites, and less on the Impergium, they'd probly come off as less flat.</div> </div> </div> </div>That might be a good point, but it varies according to where Talons are. The tribebook had them kill bastet, but respect Mokeole (in Africa) and Guralh. So, I guess that could be more focused on?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:19:00-08:00","id":316341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315672#post315672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primal Anger, Curse of Hatred, Shell (though more a sign of their control over their Rage since they can both give themselves more and shut it off), and Lash of Rage are all Metis Gifts (and just the W20 core ones) that are about the Metis focus on Rage. We can throw Madness in even though it isn't a specifically Rage theme Gift, but for a fair comparison the Red Talon Gifts: Wolf at the Door, Beastmind, Shadows of the Impergium and Howl of Death.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree with shell and madness. The former disallows the use of rage in favor of acting like turltle spirit, and I think the latter is wholey focused on the Metis being deformed and crazy. It does seem like W20 has scrapped the idea of the Red Talons having any identity beyond being cunning hunters who fight the weaver. Without the Tribebook to give them Rampage, Gorge, Mother's Rage, etc, they don't have much flavor.<br /> <br /> I'm disappointed they got rid of gifts like Avalanche and Quicksand. Unleashing nature's anger made more mystical Red Talons interesting, and now that's lost to time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That might be a good point, but it varies according to where Talons are. The tribebook had them kill bastet, but respect Mokeole (in Africa) and Guralh. So, I guess that could be more focused on?</div> </div> </div> </div>At least the overwhelming hatred of humans could be more interesting if it was meant as a uniting banner to regain the favor of the other Fera. Many of the other Fera already detest having Homid breeds in their ranks.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T09:54:51-08:00","id":316379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ExplodingJoe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=316341#post316341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree with shell and madness.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I addressed them in my post and why I included them; since they're not a straight forward as the other one's listed. Though some of the Red Talon ones are described with flavors of things like Rage, but aren't mechanically aren't all that much Rage-wise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Without the Tribebook to give them Rampage, Gorge, Mother's Rage, etc, they don't have much flavor. </div> </div> </div>There are more examples for Metis being left out in my list by not dipping into more supplements as well (Guardian of the Caern's having Badger's Heart - letting Metis screw with other character's Rage - and Twist of Fate - crappy Gift but Rage for one last attack with +10 damage dice is pretty on theme here).<br /> <br /> In the end though, I think I made my point that Red Talons are not the only splat with &quot;be in tune with Rage&quot; as a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T10:30:37-08:00","id":316389,"title":"","content":"Personally, the Red Talons have always been a paradox to me. As a tribe? I adore them. I think they're a wonderful counterpoint to the other Tribes that have managed to move on, but <i>also </i>a rather stark look at what the Garou <i>used to be </i>when the Impergium was going on and the like. They're cornered, snarling and snapping to the bitter end, cut off by ideology from their own 'brothers'.<br /> <br /> For Homids - for us - it's a <i>very </i>alien view to take. Garou aren't human but a lot of Homid have trouble letting go entirely, and the idea that the Red Talons would slaughter their Kinfolk as well as the rest of humanity is likely terrifying and doesn't paint them in a good light. But in that same vote... it's this view that makes the tribe as a whole difficult. Without digging into their Tribebook and the camps, it's likely a <i>very </i>common view that they'd happily see all of humanity gone... including Kinfolk, and ergo Homid Garou.<br /> <br /> The revised tribebook mentions that the writer asks a Red Talon if they'd kill Homid Garou - the usual response being &quot;of course not!&quot; but they'd never considered it before.<br /> <br /> As a whole, I can see why - even over Lupus in general - this view is VERY hard to pull off and even in an RP, tolerate playing. I struggle, for all I'd love to play one!<br /> <br /> Just my views!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T18:11:26-08:00","id":316783,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=315719#post315719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I wouldn't say its apologetic. I think its more the players focusing on a different aspect of the tribe than the human killing. Like, pack unity, its really hard to form packs in online games, but Talons often can bite down their dislike and pack because its what wolves -do-. That, and the tribe IS one of the best defenders of untouched wilds, that means they can get around much easier in the nature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou packs don't really have much in common with wolf packs though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-19T19:32:38-08:00","id":316876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=316783#post316783\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Garou packs don't really have much in common with wolf packs though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar enough that both need cohesion. And Red Talons are great at teamwork.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T08:53:23-08:00","id":317420,"title":"","content":"The Talons seem to get the powers normally reserved for &quot;assassin&quot; archetypes in White Wolf's other publications. Hidden Hunter lets them disguise teeth and claw marks as stab wounds... the can silence their prey... Offering of the Slain can straight up remove corpses from a crime scene. When you combine these abilities with the more late game gifts available to them - specifically the ones that allow them to shred and destroy weaver tech with ease - it seems like they're almost tailored to infiltrate cities, track down, and dispatch targets. No mess, no fuss, no need to hire a cleaner to hide the torrent of blood any other tribe would've left on the walls.<br /> <br /> Do you think its theme fitting that the Talon gift list seems to paint them almost like assassins in Garou culture?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4297-explodingjoe","name":"ExplodingJoe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4297_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-20T11:00:03-08:00","id":317574,"title":"","content":"Maybe? I mean most of those Gifts make sense as something the Red Talons would want to have. But they're not assassins.<br /> <br /> I think, if anything, the Red Talon Gifts demonstrate how muddled and poorly implemented the themes of the Red Talons are in the books. They basically seem to be based far more in line with following what a Red Talon might want to do, than be a thematic guide for what the Red Talons should be about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T06:45:21-07:00","id":1398595,"title":"","content":"Now that Matthew Dawkins have announced that this is his favorite tribe and he is &quot;just a writer&quot; of the new edition, What do you expect from the Red Talons in W5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-24T07:41:12-07:00","id":1398600,"title":"","content":"No clue. Tbh lupus Garou are the one classic WoD monster that are too alien for me to play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:50:06-07:00","id":1398808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penelope</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1398600#post1398600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No clue. Tbh lupus Garou are the one classic WoD monster that are too alien for me to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>A number of the lupus templates from the revised tribe books are some of my favorites, including the Glasswalker one who is continuously fascinated by all the new things he gets to experience, the Fianna that uses her senses and alternate perceptions to play matchmaker between Garou and Kinfolk, and the Silent Strider who lives very much in the now and has no time for regret about the past or anxiety about the future. <br /> <br /> Also my Shadow Lord Judge that I jokingly called &quot;The Gaian Inquisition&quot;, who enforced the Litany as directly and straight forward as possible, believing that nuance and interpretation were silly &quot;monkey-think&quot; ideas that weakened both individual Garou and the Garou Nation as a whole.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T09:54:30-07:00","id":1398810,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12890_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12890\" data-vbnamecard=\"12890\">No One of Consequence</a> those all sound like pretty cool characters. I\u2019ll have to check them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T11:38:53-07:00","id":1398830,"title":"","content":"And also, the lupus templates of the Red Talons are very interesting: The rascal wolf, the mystical predator, the arbitrator born in captivity, the disgraced hero or the auttum wolf are very cool characters very far from the focus in maim-burn-kill that seems limited the tribe. In fact, of the 10 templates only two could be considered extremist, the spy and the cannibal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:09:11-07:00","id":1398842,"title":"","content":"I openly admit that, had I been given the chance to write the revised Red Talon tribe book, the Ragabash character would've been called The Predator, and been someone who hunted hunters in the wilderness, with the image being a Glabro or Crinos form masked by Blur of the Milky Eye, with glowing eyes and a broken rifle in one hand and a human skull with spine still attached in the other. Because I am a total dork. <br /> <br /> (The Ahroun probably would've been The Atavism, a dire wolf throwback with the Huge Size merit.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:23:10-07:00","id":1398844,"title":"","content":"The Ahroun of the first tribebook was The Lone Wolf, a a small size super-predator with inferiority complex with the need of being the alpha and with the tragedy of having murdered is own pack in frenzy. The Ahroun of revised was the Disgraced, the fallen hero I have mentioned before. Surprisingly, neither of them is a stereotypical Red Talon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:28:28-07:00","id":1398847,"title":"","content":"Thanks guys. You\u2019ve made me see the Red Talons in a different light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-25T12:56:25-07:00","id":1398852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1398844#post1398844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Ahroun of the first tribebook was The Lone Wolf, a a small size super-predator with inferiority complex with the need of being the alpha and with the tragedy of having murdered is own pack in frenzy. The Ahroun of revised was the Disgraced, the fallen hero I have mentioned before. Surprisingly, neither of them is a stereotypical Red Talon.</div> </div> </div> </div>At some point in the near future, I'll likely end up doing a WIR thread about the first edition Werewolf templates. I remember a few of them as being down right weird. <br /> <br /> I sort of always saw my Atavism idea as being one who was driven out of his pack at a young age, both because of the underlying Rage issues that make everyone uncomfortable around pre-change Garou and because the sheer level of food he needed was putting the rest of the pack in danger of going hungry. And now he's just ludicrously elated to have found a new group where he's accepted, even if he still feels self conscious about being different from everyone else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T02:17:55-07:00","id":1398983,"title":"","content":"So, on one hand, Werewolf is all about playing an eco-fascist, and I think it's fun to try to inflate the body count with a misanthropic extremist. That gift of falsifying the cause of death is delightful.<br /> <br /> On the otherhand, and this I think is the purposeful irony of the tribe; just killing extra humans isn't actually productive. In some ways it's counter productive. If you want to destroy humanity, you either need to commit to a genocidal campaign (very costly), or you need to commit to getting humans to kill eachother, which you can't really do when you've dedicated your tribe into shutting out human influences and don't understand their triggers.<br /> <br /> How easy would it be for red talons to ignite, say, a race war? How easy would it be to escalate a the Goerge Floyd riots? You hang a few blacks, shoot a few cops, butcher a few white supremacists... wolla, America in flames with little chance of nukes. But the Red Talons don't understand how to do that because they don't really see what's going on and suggesting the idea would label you as too close to the humans/weaver. The Ratkin probably don't want to do that (The Rodens are likely as ignorant as the Tallons, and the Homids would fear the impact on their kinfolk) (as for BSD, I generally consider the Smart ones as Lazy, and the active ones as stupid, so they're not gonna go with such a plan. It might be counter to their long run interests )<br /> <br /> False flag attacks are for monkeys, not noble wolves. Even if they'd serve the RT's interests a lot better. I really like treading the RT line of 'the good wyrm' and 'the bad wyrm' for all their atrocities. But, unfortunately, the RT's lack of human understanding limits them to individually murdering more people when they have an excuse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T05:09:39-07:00","id":1399027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1398595#post1398595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that Matthew Dawkins have announced that this is his favorite tribe and he is &quot;just a writer&quot; of the new edition, What do you expect from the Red Talons in W5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not very positive, to be honest. W5 involving the Second Impegrium is already pretty much forgetting the role of Red Talons in the setting. I'm expecting they either go the MET book route of being -worse- and accepting the Dying Cubs. Or they remain the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T10:01:07-07:00","id":1399092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1398983#post1398983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, on one hand, Werewolf is all about playing an eco-fascist, and I think it's fun to try to inflate the body count with a misanthropic extremist. That gift of falsifying the cause of death is delightful.<br /> <br /> On the otherhand, and this I think is the purposeful irony of the tribe; just killing extra humans isn't actually productive. In some ways it's counter productive. If you want to destroy humanity, you either need to commit to a genocidal campaign (very costly), or you need to commit to getting humans to kill eachother, which you can't really do when you've dedicated your tribe into shutting out human influences and don't understand their triggers.<br /> <br /> How easy would it be for red talons to ignite, say, a race war? How easy would it be to escalate a the Goerge Floyd riots? You hang a few blacks, shoot a few cops, butcher a few white supremacists... wolla, America in flames with little chance of nukes. But the Red Talons don't understand how to do that because they don't really see what's going on and suggesting the idea would label you as too close to the humans/weaver. The Ratkin probably don't want to do that (The Rodens are likely as ignorant as the Tallons, and the Homids would fear the impact on their kinfolk) (as for BSD, I generally consider the Smart ones as Lazy, and the active ones as stupid, so they're not gonna go with such a plan. It might be counter to their long run interests )<br /> <br /> False flag attacks are for monkeys, not noble wolves. Even if they'd serve the RT's interests a lot better. I really like treading the RT line of 'the good wyrm' and 'the bad wyrm' for all their atrocities. But, unfortunately, the RT's lack of human understanding limits them to individually murdering more people when they have an excuse.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has been an interesting thread to follow; WtA isn't my area of expertise, but I'm always looking to learn in order to satisfy my crossover-addiction.<br /> <br /> I feel like MyWifeIsScary's post flicked on a bit of a light-bulb in my head, maybe in connection to the above remarks about Red Talons potentially being an &quot;assassin&quot; Tribe. See, it made me consider parallels with the Euthanatos Tradition of MtAs. Like the Red Talons, the Euthanatos tend to treat killing things like a hammer and tend to treat most problems like a nail. An older member of the Tradition, Senex, is said to be bothered by how his peers have become too preoccupied with violence/destruction as a solution, rather than pursuing alternatives.<br /> <br /> A possible way to 'rehabilitate' the Red Talons a bit is to have their modern Tribal theme of &quot;kill the tainted monkeys&quot; be a degradation/corruption of their original purpose. The Red Talons are not the Tribe of hating humans; the Red Talons are the Tribe of preserving lupus Kinfolk and keeping the &quot;wolf perspective&quot; represented within the broader culture of the Garou Nation. The decision to accept lupus Kinfolk and Garou exclusively was, originally, not about seeing humans as inferior, but instead making sure that one Tribe always viewed wolf Kin as a priority. Red Talons may have always been primitives who rejected tools and the trappings of 'civilization,' but they may have once been able to tolerate and understand it enough to go among humans and influence them in less violent ways, teaching them to appreciate the perspectives and strengths of wolves, working as a mediator between the two breeds the way shamans mediate between the material and spirit worlds.<br /> <br /> The modern Tribe's active hatred of humans, instead of being the 'natural state' of the Tribe, is more of a response to how history has turned out, an overreaction, and a mistaking of what was supposed to be merely one means (killing humans to defend wolves, when necessary) as instead being the end-unto-itself (kill all the humans, because everything bad is their fault). Given the relationship between humans and the decline of the wolf population, a Tribe that views protecting wolves as their sacred duty would likely be inclined to develop poor views of humanity. Of course, that would likely be as much a failure on their part, and the Garou as a whole, as it is humanity's, but it makes their perspective more relatable, and provides an idea of what a more moderate Red Talon might look like.<br /> <br /> <br /> Regarding the previous debate about whether or not Red Talons especially represent the Wyld, and whether or not humanity's &quot;strengths&quot; are &quot;natural,&quot; I would like to quickly point out that while it's fair to say that human use of tools and social organization is indeed &quot;natural,&quot; that's not the same as saying it is &quot;of the Wyld.&quot; The comparison to ants makes it especially clear: ants are of the Weaver, not the Wyld. That being said, I do agree with the idea that the concept of the Wyld does seem to go beyond &quot;nature.&quot; If we want to equate the Red Talon perspective with &quot;nature,&quot; perhaps their views (originally, at least) should not be regarded as closest to the Wyld, but instead to Gaia as embodying the balance of the &quot;natural cycle&quot; of birth, life, and death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T16:21:21-07:00","id":1399160,"title":"","content":"Since this is now talking about ways to develop the tribe, I'll <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/912624-heretical-thoughts-on-griffin-and-the-red-talons\">link to a thread</a> I started years ago on &quot;heretical thoughts&quot; about Griffin and the Red Talons. It didn't present a cohesive alternate to the tribe. Instead, it discussed aspects of myth and legend surrounding Griffin, and how that could be used to give the tribe more depth and increase playability. So it was discussion of options that players and STs may want to consider when using the tribe. The thread got derailed at the end, but I know many people found the first few pages helpful.<br /> <br /> I've certainly used most of these points in developing the tribe in my own chronicles, especially in explaining why the Red Talons act as they do, and resolving some of the things that seem contradictory about the tribe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-26T22:58:32-07:00","id":1399215,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1399092#post1399092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A possible way to 'rehabilitate' the Red Talons a bit is to have their modern Tribal theme of &quot;kill the tainted monkeys&quot; be a degradation/corruption of their original purpose. The Red Talons are not the Tribe of hating humans; the Red Talons are the Tribe of preserving lupus Kinfolk and keeping the &quot;wolf perspective&quot; represented within the broader culture of the Garou Nation. The decision to accept lupus Kinfolk and Garou exclusively was, originally, not about seeing humans as inferior, but instead making sure that one Tribe always viewed wolf Kin as a priority. Red Talons may have always been primitives who rejected tools and the trappings of 'civilization,' but they may have once been able to tolerate and understand it enough to go among humans and influence them in less violent ways, teaching them to appreciate the perspectives and strengths of wolves, working as a mediator between the two breeds the way shamans mediate between the material and spirit worlds.<br /> <br /> The modern Tribe's active hatred of humans, instead of being the 'natural state' of the Tribe, is more of a response to how history has turned out, an overreaction, and a mistaking of what was supposed to be merely one means (killing humans to defend wolves, when necessary) as instead being the end-unto-itself (kill all the humans, because everything bad is their fault). Given the relationship between humans and the decline of the wolf population, a Tribe that views protecting wolves as their sacred duty would likely be inclined to develop poor views of humanity. Of course, that would likely be as much a failure on their part, and the Garou as a whole, as it is humanity's, but it makes their perspective more relatable, and provides an idea of what a more moderate Red Talon might look like.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is the perspective behind the tribebooks, in fact. Most of the Red Talons are more engaged in preserve the few natural areas that remain that in to kill humans. Furthermore, genocide it is a human thing. Most of the Red Talons could think that if there would not exist the humans, they would not have theses problems. No humans, no wyrm and no weaver domination. And that is in fact very true, but they lack the compromise, the organization and the resources required to do &quot;anything else&quot; that some unconnected murders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T03:57:59-07:00","id":1399246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1399215#post1399215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Furthermore, genocide it is a human thing.</div> </div> </div> </div> It is not, humans are just more capable and likely to write it down. Predators in the wild kill the children of their rivals, and the adults if they think they can pu\u013al it off. Grey wolves consistently target bear cubs and foxes. The wars of rage were successful because of the human side, but they sparked over the animal sides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:29:08-07:00","id":1399250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1399246#post1399246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It is not, humans are just more capable and likely to write it down. Predators in the wild kill the children of their rivals, and the adults if they think they can pu\u013al it off. Grey wolves consistently target bear cubs and foxes. The wars of rage were successful because of the human side, but they sparked over the animal sides.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well....yeah. But thats just nature. Genocide is where you plan to intentionally wipe another group from the face of the earth. Animals simply don't do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:47:26-07:00","id":1399256,"title":"","content":"They would if they could.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:47:27-07:00","id":1399257,"title":"","content":"Animals kill to eat, to reproduce or to protect their territory or children. But animals do not wipe out an entire race or species as humans do (buffalo, for example).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:48:30-07:00","id":1399258,"title":"","content":"IDK, I think killing every bear you can in the region so you don't have to worry about bears is pretty genocidal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T04:50:21-07:00","id":1399259,"title":"","content":"And aside the game, what animal is doing that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T05:29:17-07:00","id":1399267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1399259#post1399259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And aside the game, what animal is doing that?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> He's gonna say wolves. But its blatantly incorrect. They'll opportunistically prey on young bears if there are few other options available and they will drive problematic adult bears from their territory if possible but they do not and never have systematically tracked down and exterminate every single bear in the region. In fact there are a number of wolf territories where bears are essentially unmolested as they act as a buffer against coyotes or rival wolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T07:05:19-07:00","id":1399283,"title":"","content":"Alright then.<br /> <br /> Cats<br /> <br /> Checkmate &quot;only humans commit genocide people&quot;<br /> <br /> Edit: So I looked it up again. <br /> Yeah, wolves surplus kill bears. They will kill bears without eating all of them. They will drag bears out of dens to kill them. It's oppertunistic genocide for better territory. If wolves think they can kill bears without too much trouble, they will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 06-27-2020, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T14:14:18-07:00","id":1399374,"title":"","content":"Actually animals cause other animals to go extinct all the time. Usually that is the case of invasive species that humans brought with them, but in other cases when an animal population are able to travel to a new land itself, the same result occurs. Cats, for example, have wiped out many species of birds and small animals particularly on islands and Australia. Discarded Burmese Pythons are doing the same in the Everglades.<br /> <br /> This generally occurs when a predator is introduced that native animals didn't evolve with, and they lack the natural defenses. But sometimes it's a non-predator that is simply better suited for survival in that environment than the native animals, and they outcompete them for those resources and drive them out which leads to population decline, then collapse, and then extinction. Sometimes this is due to natural climate change, and the environment has changed sufficient enough for animal populations to migrate. The last is probably the reason for the earliest extinctions in the Quaternary Extinction Event (although extinctions that occurred later are likely due to humans).<br /> <br /> That doesn't change the fact that humans, because of our success in living in many environments and changing habitats, are responsible for a vastly accelerated extinction rate. But before humans, there was still a normal extinction rate, and other animals are a part of that cause.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T14:26:56-07:00","id":1399382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1399257#post1399257\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Animals kill to eat, to reproduce or to protect their territory or children. But animals do not wipe out an entire race or species as humans do (buffalo, for example).</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, getting away from the term genocide, since that's a fairly loaded word to try to apply to non-humans based on our linguistic biases, there's a more useful term to use: surplus killing.<br /> <br /> It's a pretty easy to understand phrase. Surplus killing is when an animal kills another animal in excess (or surplus since it started focused on predator-prey killing) of their survival needs. Humans are, obviously, notorious surplus killers. We do it to each other and other animals all the time.<br /> <br /> However, surplus killing is exceedingly common in nature. The evolutionary history of the behavior is relatively safe to assume: animals that evolve to kill more than they need are more likely to have killed enough if times get tough, while animals that kill just enough to survive are constantly at risk of not having killed enough to survive (not just eat, territorial competition, mating competition, etc.).<br /> <br /> For example, spotted hyenas murder lion cubs and adolescents whenever they have a chance. There's no consideration for the lion pride's health, or sharing resources. The hyenas might not be trying to wipe lions out, but they'll kill lions as hard as possible to ensure lions pose as little of a threat as possible even to the point of wiping out a pride if they can. Every dead lion is one less lion the hyenas have to compete with during difficult hunting seasons, so hyenas proactively kill lions even when there isn't direct competition. Lions, of course, kill back too.<br /> <br /> Dolphins are one of the most notoriously murder happy species besides humans because they kill animals for no reason we can actually explain. Besides being highly violent creatures in their internal socialization, dolphins have been repeatedly documented killing other species that aren't threats to them; no food competition, no territoriality, no physical threat to the dolphins. Since they mostly seem to target smaller porpoises, one of the best guesses besides &quot;they're just violent assholes,&quot; is that they're practicing their murder skills for killing the young of rival dolphins. Running around murdering smaller animals like that is something humans associate with violent sociopaths. <br /> <br /> And yes, wolves are well know surplus killers too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T14:44:57-07:00","id":1399392,"title":"","content":"There's this sort of pervasive belief among people, that nature is harmonious and balanced. It emphatically is not. It's a whole bunch of organisms trying to maximize their survival through whatever mechanisms available to them, regardless of context. What we see in a stable ecosystem is a hard-fought equilibrium, born of various factors that got good enough at working around each other that nothing goes extinct. This doesn't mean those organisms won't wreck that ecosystem the moment the situation changes.<br /> <br /> Just as rabbits will <i>literally</i> fuck their environment to death, regardless of utility, a predator or even just particularly deadly prey animal would destroy an entire species given the chance. They follow their instincts, regardless of utility.<br /> <br /> <br /> Although I think we're missing the werewolf for the fur, if you catch my drift. Regardless of a regular wolf's capacity of genocide, the Red Talons - as a tribe and culture - are not mere brute beasts. They have the capacity for abstract thinking and long-term planning that their kinfolk do not. If they decided that humans were such a problem, they could conclude that genocide is the only solution. Some, indeed, do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T15:15:25-07:00","id":1399404,"title":"","content":"One of the best parts of Red Talon writing for me, and one that is important in seeing the tribe as more complex, is that they are very much architects of their own misery.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons could have affected the Litany, they could have joined the discussion. But they refused because they saw it as too human. When the Litany then forbid eating human flesh, they complained that they had to obey it and developed rites to cheat it.<br /> <br /> Then there is the fact that some Red Talons have chosen to become African Cape Dog or Dingo to aid Gaia, while others complain about those garou not being 'true' Talons. The tribe has an interesting take on adaptation vs tradition. In that, some Talons adapt easily without sacrificing their morals, while others are so adamant that they live by the old ways as to harm their chances of survival.<br /> <br /> In that, Red Talons are actually very human. It was their refusal to adapt and change that made them such an isolated tribe, it was their perception of the world that drives them to defy Litany out of sheer stubbornness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T16:03:35-07:00","id":1399418,"title":"","content":"They are indeed a tribe full of ironies. <br /> <br /> It also seems like they should get wiped out by other garou due to kinfolk disputes. all tribes are desperate for more lupus kin but RT are especially demanding. But from a duel/frontal conflict point of view they're a lot weaker than the other tribes in terms of silver and combat gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T17:19:32-07:00","id":1399434,"title":"","content":"Iron-y Talons. Red, from rust.<br /> <br /> Oddly, one of the Talons' early distinctions was being super into killing vampires; in fact, the 1e writeup mentioned that they have this aim even above that of killing humans. Then the Silent Striders sort of stole that thunder, courtesy of the Setite rivalry and a Gift geared toward keeping blood points on lockdown.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T19:07:43-07:00","id":1399465,"title":"","content":"Yeah. It was the word genocide that was the trip up, introduced species like cats/foxes etc. here in Oz have decimated native species but they don't draw up plans and specifically target individual communities to be exterminated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T06:13:37-07:00","id":1400716,"title":"","content":"Fully admitting my inexperience with W:tA here, so please feel free to correct me if/when I get something horribly wrong. Ahem!<br /> <br /> The Talons seem indeed limited in scope. They're dominated by their &quot;Kill the Apes!&quot; theme, easily overshadowing anything else they might bring to the table. Kill all humans, kill most humans, kill some humans... nothing not connected to ape-killing in sight. For the record, I personally despise the Ratkin for much the same reasons and find reducing an animal that appears to have profited from the rise of cities themselves, nevermind one that can be affectionate, smart, and overall great pets, a disservice.<br /> <br /> Plus I dislike WW's murderfactions. But that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> Added to that, exploring internal fractures among the Tribe kinda goes against what they try to be at their core, doesn't it? Wolves don't have political parties. That's a human thing. The Red Talons aren't just wolves, sure, but they're pretending really hard that they are, and that means adopting a limited perspective because deep introspection isn't wolf-ish. That they then complain about reality not conforming to their wishes is very human again, as others pointed out...<br /> <br /> They also don't have a cultural hook. Get, Silent Striders, Fianna, Furies, Uktena, Wendigo, Siberakh, Shadow Lords... Nobody can tell me &quot;viking werewolves&quot; isn't a huge draw for the Fenrir, for example.<br /> <br /> If it were up to me, I might do something completely left-field with the Red Talons. Something crazy. Like, say, introduce a faction working on rituals to turn ordinary dogs into kinfolk. Yeah, it would be an admission of defeat in a sense, but dying for your pride is a HUMAN goal. Beasts are about survival.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T09:18:48-07:00","id":1400760,"title":"","content":"Ratkin are the best splat. Change my mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T10:08:49-07:00","id":1400773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1400716#post1400716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fully admitting my inexperience with W:tA here, so please feel free to correct me if/when I get something horribly wrong. Ahem!<br /> <br /> The Talons seem indeed limited in scope. They're dominated by their &quot;Kill the Apes!&quot; theme, easily overshadowing anything else they might bring to the table. Kill all humans, kill most humans, kill some humans... nothing not connected to ape-killing in sight. For the record, I personally despise the Ratkin for much the same reasons and find reducing an animal that appears to have profited from the rise of cities themselves, nevermind one that can be affectionate, smart, and overall great pets, a disservice.<br /> <br /> Plus I dislike WW's murderfactions. But that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> Added to that, exploring internal fractures among the Tribe kinda goes against what they try to be at their core, doesn't it? Wolves don't have political parties. That's a human thing. The Red Talons aren't just wolves, sure, but they're pretending really hard that they are, and that means adopting a limited perspective because deep introspection isn't wolf-ish. That they then complain about reality not conforming to their wishes is very human again, as others pointed out...<br /> <br /> They also don't have a cultural hook. Get, Silent Striders, Fianna, Furies, Uktena, Wendigo, Siberakh, Shadow Lords... Nobody can tell me &quot;viking werewolves&quot; isn't a huge draw for the Fenrir, for example.<br /> <br /> If it were up to me, I might do something completely left-field with the Red Talons. Something crazy. Like, say, introduce a faction working on rituals to turn ordinary dogs into kinfolk. Yeah, it would be an admission of defeat in a sense, but dying for your pride is a HUMAN goal. Beasts are about survival.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing about Red Talons is, indeed, that they are being very human about things while they think they are being wolves. Red Talons actively refuse to engage with a human mind.. but that human mind is the reason why they are complain about the Litany in the first place.<br /> <br /> Red Talons are not thinking like wolves, in truth. Actual wolves won't whine about old-days, they adapt. They don't force limitations for themselves, they don't make an infirmed choice what is 'acceptable' for a wolf. Red Talons do, they limits themselves while saying 'wolves' act the same. They have writing (but not HUMAN writing), culture and septs like all garou.<br /> <br /> Red Talons are the best when they are serving as a reminder of willful ignorance and yet what a lot of garou have lost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:19:32-07:00","id":1400856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1400760#post1400760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ratkin are the best splat. Change my mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>They had some awesome concepts. Munchmausen are pure love. Now, if only they could get away more from their iron-clad Gaia-given duty, but then, W:tA had that problem at its core, how the major cosmological aspects were more or less cut and dried, if I remember correctly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T17:31:08-07:00","id":1400861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1400773#post1400773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing about Red Talons is, indeed, that they are being very human about things while they think they are being wolves. Red Talons actively refuse to engage with a human mind.. but that human mind is the reason why they are complain about the Litany in the first place.<br /> <br /> Red Talons are not thinking like wolves, in truth. Actual wolves won't whine about old-days, they adapt. They don't force limitations for themselves, they don't make an infirmed choice what is 'acceptable' for a wolf. Red Talons do, they limits themselves while saying 'wolves' act the same. They have writing (but not HUMAN writing), culture and septs like all garou.<br /> <br /> Red Talons are the best when they are serving as a reminder of willful ignorance and yet what a lot of garou have lost.</div> </div> </div> </div>As a symbol, it works fine. Is it interesting as a playable character concept, though? Is it enough? It doesn't seem to be for many, hence the dearth of Red Talon players in comparison.<br /> <br /> Sidenote, does anyone here know much about what the Talons think of domestic dogs? Is there anything at all? Their feral ancestors may have died out, but they're still awfully close to wolves in general. Closer at any rate than MARSUPIALS. If I were a Red Talon, I'd have some very conflicting feelings about the human-friendly traitors to wolf-kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T19:00:21-07:00","id":1400877,"title":"","content":"Well I know it's fairly well established that to be referred to as a 'dog' is considered an insult amongst the Garou. Given that the Red Talons are the ones most dedicated to the Wyld, feral nature, and self-declared opposition to humanity... I doubt they hold dogs in very high regard.<br /> <br /> At best I imagine they might see dogs as cunning survivors who forfeited their true nature to endure... but I see this as a very minority opinion amongst those of the Whelp's Compromise. I would imagine that most Red Talons see dogs as victims of humanity and Weaver taint at best or as traitorous quislings at worse.<br /> <br /> Ultimately I see them seeing the current form of dogs as tragic figures who have been perverted and mutated by Weaver taint and who have forfeit their spiritual birthright through accepting Man's yoke.<br /> <br /> Feral dogs might skate by but they're on thin ice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:09:57-07:00","id":1400885,"title":"","content":"All good points. And good examples, I think, of exploring different viewpoints in and from their limited worldview.<br /> <br /> The Red Talons are doomed to think. They SHOULD have a greater variety of opinion than they admit to themselves and, especially, to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:27:35-07:00","id":1400890,"title":"","content":"I assume Red Talons see any domesticated animals as &quot;traitors&quot;. I don't think they see the animals as guilty - they know they're just animals and don't have choice - but they see domestication as a perversion enabled by the Weaver or Wyrm, and feel a mix of anger and sadness at such animals, and hate humans even more for it. But dogs especially, since they are often the enemies of wolves - protecting the flock and helping human hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:38:23-07:00","id":1400892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1400716#post1400716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fully admitting my inexperience with W:tA here, so please feel free to correct me if/when I get something horribly wrong. Ahem!<br /> <br /> The Talons seem indeed limited in scope. They're dominated by their &quot;Kill the Apes!&quot; theme, easily overshadowing anything else they might bring to the table. Kill all humans, kill most humans, kill some humans... nothing not connected to ape-killing in sight. For the record, I personally despise the Ratkin for much the same reasons and find reducing an animal that appears to have profited from the rise of cities themselves, nevermind one that can be affectionate, smart, and overall great pets, a disservice.<br /> <br /> Plus I dislike WW's murderfactions. But that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> Added to that, exploring internal fractures among the Tribe kinda goes against what they try to be at their core, doesn't it? Wolves don't have political parties. That's a human thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Captive wolves play politics to determine hierarchies because their wild-living family-based grouping gets disrupted and leaves unanswered questions of social organization. This would also presumably happen normally among the Garou, given the inability to breed with each other to the effect of starting families, even if they didn't turn into humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Red Talons aren't just wolves, sure, but they're pretending really hard that they are, and that means adopting a limited perspective because deep introspection isn't wolf-ish. </div> </div> </div>Correction, the writers thought that it wasn't very wolf-like. The writers were also bound by prejudices from before good research on wolf cognition, though, so we could easily change that given various data points like the survey of behavior in Are We Smart Enough to Know How Smart Animals Are or Mama's Last Hug. Contrary to memes spread by game designers, there is no &quot;eternal now&quot; that ensnares the thought processes of wild animals, for example, but writing so that everything complicated is couched in terms of scents and tastes first and foremost might be a bit trying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That they then complain about reality not conforming to their wishes is very human again, as others pointed out...<br /> <br /> They also don't have a cultural hook. Get, Silent Striders, Fianna, Furies, Uktena, Wendigo, Siberakh, Shadow Lords... Nobody can tell me &quot;viking werewolves&quot; isn't a huge draw for the Fenrir, for example. </div> </div> </div>First, the Fenrir aren't actually Viking werewolves. They're werewolves that incidentally lived around/preferentially killed vikings and hate the pre-Christian Norse/Germanic religions with a fierce passion. Secondly, this can work to the Talons' advantage by setting up an anti-mythology, a cultural standard that broadly resembles human mythology but reversed. The Fenrir already do this by turning Norse/Germanic folklore on its head and presenting Odin as a villainous bastard and foul necromancer, their tribe's eternal enemy, and Valhalla as a hall full of spirits that the tribe will have to do battle with. You just need to go deeper into this, though admittedly not having connections to a specific human cultural group does make the question of where to start rather open-ended.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If it were up to me, I might do something completely left-field with the Red Talons. Something crazy. Like, say, introduce a faction working on rituals to turn ordinary dogs into kinfolk. Yeah, it would be an admission of defeat in a sense, but dying for your pride is a HUMAN goal. Beasts are about survival. </div> </div> </div>Dogs metaphysically cannot be kin or changers of any kind because they're domesticated. It takes four generations of feral living to undo this, bare minimum; usually, that means breeding with wolves as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T20:51:22-07:00","id":1400894,"title":"","content":"Well, what is a dog? It is a wolf that has been forcefully physically and mentally warped into a tool or toy for and by humans. I don't think they would blame the dogs....why would they? But humans for doing that to them? You betcha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-03T21:09:50-07:00","id":1400896,"title":"","content":"I know they're not actually vikings. I still think the idea is a big draw for some, even if it's not historically accurate either in- or out-of-universe.<br /> <br /> As for the other points: That all implies work needed by the writers, doesn't it? Going back to how they're not attractive NOW as player characters.<br /> <br /> On the topic of kinfolk, that's A) writer fiat and B) I did say a ritual. That's kinda the opposite of waiting for it to develop naturally. The Spirals managed to make a Metis fertile. Pentex made werecockroaches. At least it would be something different from &quot;Kill the Apes!&quot;. Even if it's ultimately doomed to fail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26275,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","user":"Konigheim Horror","date":". 07-04-2020, 12:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T04:20:29-07:00","id":1400933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1400896#post1400896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know they're not actually vikings. I still think the idea is a big draw for some, even if it's not historically accurate either in- or out-of-universe.<br /> <br /> As for the other points: That all implies work needed by the writers, doesn't it? Going back to how they're not attractive NOW as player characters.<br /> <br /> On the topic of kinfolk, that's A) writer fiat and B) I did say a ritual. That's kinda the opposite of waiting for it to develop naturally. The Spirals managed to make a Metis fertile. Pentex made werecockroaches. At least it would be something different from &quot;Kill the Apes!&quot;. Even if it's ultimately doomed to fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spiral actually didn't make metis fertile, they just make a LOT of them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T05:24:02-07:00","id":1400940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1400933#post1400933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spiral actually didn't make metis fertile, they just make a LOT of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a scenario in Times of Judgement where the Perfect Metis impregnates Zhyzhak. Though I got some details wrong; it's wasn't the BSD (who tried to get Metis fertile for a while now), it was the fallen Glasswalkers under Cockroach.<br /> <br /> I do understand if people scoff at ToJ scenarios for being, at times, pretty out there. You'll get no complaints from me. They're written for dramatic effect first and foremost. Trying to make Metis fertile, that does go back to Book of the Wyrm though, if I recall.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-04T22:16:02-07:00","id":1401057,"title":"","content":"The Spirals didn't make a metis fertile. The Perfect Metis was presumably born that way, and Zhyzhak is homid. And also wildly out of character in that scenario.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-05T06:12:29-07:00","id":1401097,"title":"","content":"I don't remember anything about the Perfect Metis being naturally fertile... of course, I could be wrong. Do you disagree with the idea that the BSD were *trying* to make Metis fertile, though? That was in the original Book of the Wyrm. And it did not say there &quot;This will never work&quot;, it said &quot;If they succeed, the Garou Nation is done&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that it's only one idea to give the Red Talons more to do in the eyes of players than sulk and kill humans for pissing in the woods. That's what it comes down to for many, and it's a crying shame.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-06T11:11:28-07:00","id":1401372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/299851-red-talons-the-throw-away-tribe?p=1401097#post1401097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember anything about the Perfect Metis being naturally fertile... of course, I could be wrong. Do you disagree with the idea that the BSD were *trying* to make Metis fertile, though? That was in the original Book of the Wyrm. And it did not say there &amp;quot;This will never work&amp;quot;, it said &amp;quot;If they succeed, the Garou Nation is done&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Nevermind that it's only one idea to give the Red Talons more to do in the eyes of players than sulk and kill humans for pissing in the woods. That's what it comes down to for many, and it's a crying shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>Without explicit text to elaborate, I've always taken it as the Perfect Metis being born fertile. The whole point is 'a Metis with no (discernible) flaws,' and sterility seems like an evident flaw from a Garou or biological/evolutionary perspective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","user":"Kharnov","date":". 07-09-2020, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}